{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SXhMG8DC58tVbjieH2qSHx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.handoff\n2\t  \"Stage 1 of the post-M5 hardening (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md\n3\t   section 14.1): the kept-cursor handoff -- one blocked or halted task\n4\t   exported as canonical bytes, resumed as a fresh task on another host.\n5\t\n6\t   `export-task` is the lift of 14.1.2: it validates the safepoint and\n7\t   the empty ready queue, captures the ordered waits without polling\n8\t   them, walks the reachable graph with ONE source-resource-to-cell\n9\t   map (`yin.vm.completion`'s fixed point over the whole frame set, so\n10\t   two waiters on one cell lift to one UCF cell and a cell a closure or\n11\t   the store also reaches shares the same id), derives every dynamic\n12\t   reason and pending variant from the OBSERVED wait entry -- never\n13\t   from the static `:yin.safepoint/kinds` at the pc, which only gates\n14\t   eligibility (`yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md` section 8) -- closes the\n15\t   requirements, validates the whole body, and answers it as canonical\n16\t   CBOR bytes under their content address.\n17\t\n18\t   `resume-task` is the lower, and its reader is version-aware (M-next\n19\t   D7): the version-1 decode is tried first -- `dao.jing.cbor` canonical\n20\t   bytes, whose decoder refuses the stream codec's tag-39 identifiers --\n21\t   then the stage-1 `dao.stream.cbor` decode; the codec that accepted\n22\t   the bytes decides which body version they may carry (version 1 in\n23\t   jing bytes, version 0 in stream bytes, enforced as\n24\t   `:yin.k/profile-mismatch` before the address check), a version-1\n25\t   body then runs the custody inspector (`yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint`) over\n26\t   its claimed address, and a failure at any step is never\n27\t   reinterpreted through the other codec.  It checks stamp, grammar,\n28\t   references and code hashes before anything is installed;\n29\t   attach each stream identity once through its carried descriptor;\n30\t   allocate one fresh private resource per logical cell and stream;\n31\t   re-seal every reference under the receiving task; restore the store\n32\t   slice, the module stores, the counter and the parked records, then\n33\t   the ordered waits; and answer the runnable machine only after all\n34\t   restoration passes.  A failed lower installs nothing partially\n35\t   runnable: refusals are total.\n36\t\n37\t   The transfer seam is the same composition pair `yin.vm.ucf.remote`\n38\t   defined: `serve!` (the exporter's remote-table entry, so the source\n39\t   keeps serving the stream) and `attach!` (the receiver's dispatch).\n40\t   Version 0 resumes as a fork. Version 1 restores a running root only\n41\t   with composition-supplied grant evidence and protection declarations;\n42\t   halted results restore ended, and install children carry the gate only.\n43\t\n44\t   Halt is a result, never a frame: the halted body carries the result\n45\t   and no wait at all.  An explicit park is the no-wait shape: the\n46\t   parked record travels in the scheduler slice under its own id and\n47\t   no pending is minted for it.  An install waiter travels beside its\n48\t   whole child -- the child's own handoff body, phase and response --\n49\t   or the export refuses; an install name alone reconstructs nothing.\"\n50\t  (:require [clojure.set :as set]\n51\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n52\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as jing.cbor]\n53\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n54\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n55\t            [dao.stream.cbor :as cbor]\n56\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n57\t            [yin.vm.code :as code]\n58\t            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as walker]\n59\t            [yin.vm.completion :as completion]\n60\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dcode]\n61\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n62\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-effects :as reffects]\n63\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as register]\n64\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as stack]\n65\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n66\t            [yin.vm.integer.host :as integer-host]\n67\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n68\t            [yin.vm.ucf :as ucf]\n69\t            [yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint :as checkpoint]\n70\t            [yin.vm.ucf.custody :as custody]\n71\t            [yin.vm.ucf.remote :as ucf.remote]\n72\t            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n73\t\n74\t\n75\t(def handoff-tag\n76\t  \"The S7.5.1 tag of one handoff body.\"\n77\t  :yin.k/handoff)\n78\t\n79\t\n80\t(def handoff-version\n81\t  \"The body versions this namespace's reader speaks: version 0, the\n82\t   frozen stage-1 wire the lower still emits, version 1, the custody\n83\t   amendment (section 14.3) whose canonical bytes are dao.jing.cbor's,\n84\t   and version 2, the four-profile amendment\n85\t   (docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md),\n86\t   also in dao.jing.cbor bytes.  Which a body may carry is decided by\n87\t   the codec that accepted its bytes -- the version-aware reader's gate,\n88\t   before the tag grammar and before any address or restoration check --\n89\t   and a body of any other version, absent or not of the integer kind,\n90\t   is refused with :yin.k/profile-mismatch.  Version 2 is dispatched\n91\t   by exact integer kind and structural role, never by `>= 1`: it is\n92\t   selected at export by the composition's `:version 2` option.\"\n93\t  #{0 1 2})\n94\t\n95\t\n96\t;; =============================================================================\n97\t;; Refusal vocabulary (S7.9): every failure is a data outcome\n98\t;; =============================================================================\n99\t\n100\t(defn- refuse!\n101\t  [status data]\n102\t  (throw (ex-info (str \"Handoff refused: \" (name status))\n103\t                  (merge {:yin.k/status status} data))))\n104\t\n105\t\n106\t(defn- non-portable!\n107\t  [kind data]\n108\t  (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable (assoc data :yin.k/kind kind)))\n109\t\n110\t\n111\t(defn- unsatisfied!\n112\t  ([] (unsatisfied! nil))\n113\t  ([identity]\n114\t   (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied\n115\t            (cond-> {} (some? identity)\n116\t                    (assoc :dao.stream/identity identity)))))\n117\t\n118\t\n119\t(defn- undecodable!\n120\t  [data]\n121\t  (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable data))\n122\t\n123\t\n124\t(defn- not-at-safepoint!\n125\t  [pc]\n126\t  (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint {:yin.k/pc pc}))\n127\t\n128\t\n129\t(defn- outcome\n130\t  \"The S7.9 data outcome exception `e` carries, or nil.\"\n131\t  [e]\n132\t  (let [d (ex-data e)]\n133\t    (when (and (map? d) (contains? d :yin.k/status)) d)))\n134\t\n135\t\n136\t(defn- call!\n137\t  \"Run `f`, answering its value, or the data outcome it refused with.\n138\t   A throw with no outcome vocabulary is a defect, not a refusal: it\n139\t   propagates.\"\n140\t  [f]\n141\t  (try (f)\n142\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n143\t         (if-let [d (outcome e)] d (throw e)))))\n144\t\n145\t\n146\t;; =============================================================================\n147\t;; The one cell map (14.1.2 lift step 2): minted across the WHOLE set\n148\t;; =============================================================================\n149\t\n150\t(defn- scalar?\n151\t  [x]\n152\t  (or (nil? x) (boolean? x)\n153\t      (and (number? x) (not (integer-host/big-carrier? x)))\n154\t      (string? x) (keyword? x) (symbol? x)))\n155\t\n156\t\n157\t(defn- local-identity\n158\t  \"The identity `h` itself declares, when its descriptor answers ok;\n159\t   nil otherwise -- the best name a refusal can give before `serve!`.\"\n160\t  [h]\n161\t  (let [d (when (stream/descriptor? h) (stream/descriptor h))]\n162\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome d))\n163\t      (:dao.stream/identity d))))\n164\t\n165\t\n166\t(defn- marker-for!\n167\t  \"The UCF stream marker for the stream resource `id` of `vm`, minted\n168\t   through the exporter's own table (`serve!`) once per resource: the\n169\t   descriptor serve! answers, never a handle.  A resource id the\n170\t   private table does not hold is a forged reference; `serve!` here is\n171\t   the keyed form `(serve! id handle)` of `export-task`, so the answer\n172\t   is retained under the resource id, never under the handle.  A stream the\n173\t   table cannot serve is unsatisfied, naming the identity where one is\n174\t   known.  Two resources of one identity mint two markers that name\n175\t   the one identity -- the lower attaches per identity, once.  Under\n176\t   the ordering scratch the marker is seeded by the resource id and\n177\t   nothing is asked: a sort comparison serves no stream and mints no\n178\t   identity, exactly as it mints no cell number.\"\n179\t  [vm serve! found id]\n180\t  (if (:ordering @found)\n181\t    (or (get-in @found [:markers id])\n182\t        (let [m {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/stream\n183\t                 :dao.stream/identity id\n184\t                 :dao.stream/descriptor {:yin.k/hint :ordering}}]\n185\t          (swap! found assoc-in [:markers id] m)\n186\t          m))\n187\t    (let [handle (get (:resources vm) id)]\n188\t      (if (nil? handle)\n189\t        (non-portable! :forged-resource-reference {:yin.k/hint id})\n190\t        (or (get-in @found [:markers id])\n191\t            (if-let [marker (ucf.remote/lift-marker (partial serve! id)\n192\t                                                    handle)]\n193\t              (do (swap! found assoc-in [:markers id] marker) marker)\n194\t              (unsatisfied! (local-identity handle))))))))\n195\t\n196\t\n197\t(defn- portable-cursor\n198\t  \"The kept cursor when it survives a round trip through the body's\n199\t   own canonical codec -- encoded, decoded back, equal -- which is what\n200\t   the :dao.stream.remote/v1 claim means for this body.  nil when it\n201\t   does not, so no cell is ever published over an unpublishable\n202\t   cursor.\"\n203\t  [kept]\n204\t  (try (let [b (cbor/encode kept)]\n205\t         (when (= kept (cbor/decode b)) kept))\n206\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n207\t\n208\t\n209\t(defn- cell-at!\n210\t  \"The logical cursor cell for an explicit kept position on the stream\n211\t   resource `stream-id` (UCF 7.5.3), minted once per `key` across the\n212\t   WHOLE export: two references through one key share one cell id.\n213\t   Cell ids are lift-local identities, never content or position\n214\t   hashes.  Under the ordering scratch (`:ordering`) the id IS the key\n215\t   -- the resource id, or the position pair, the very identity the cell\n216\t   table itself keys by -- so a sort comparison never mints a number\n217\t   and no traversal order can change which distinct cursor sorts\n218\t   first.\"\n219\t  [vm serve! found key stream-id kept]\n220\t  (or (get-in @found [:cell-of key])\n221\t      (let [marker (marker-for! vm serve! found stream-id)]\n222\t        (if (some? (portable-cursor kept))\n223\t          (let [cid (if (:ordering @found)\n224\t                      key\n225\t                      (or (get-in @found [:recovery-cell-ids key])\n226\t                          (keyword \"yin.k\" (str \"c-\" (count (:cells @found))))))]\n227\t            (swap! found\n228\t                   (fn [acc]\n229\t                     (-> acc\n230\t                         (assoc-in [:cell-of key] cid)\n231\t                         (assoc-in [:cells cid]\n232\t                                   {:yin.k/stream marker\n233\t                                    :yin.k/position kept}))))\n234\t            cid)\n235\t          (unsatisfied! (:dao.stream/identity marker))))))\n236\t\n237\t\n238\t(defn- cell-for!\n239\t  \"The cell the cursor-cell resource `id` lifts to: the entry's kept\n240\t   position on its own stream.  A key naming no resource is a forged\n241\t   reference.\"\n242\t  [vm serve! found id]\n243\t  (let [cell (get (:resources vm) id)]\n244\t    (if (nil? cell)\n245\t      (non-portable! :forged-resource-reference {:yin.k/hint id})\n246\t      (cell-at! vm serve! found id (:stream-id cell) (:cursor cell)))))\n247\t\n248\t\n249\t;; =============================================================================\n250\t;; The found map and the canonical order of a version-1 export\n251\t;; =============================================================================\n252\t\n253\t(defn- new-found\n254\t  []\n255\t  {:cells {} :cell-of {} :markers {} :stores #{} :segments #{}})\n256\t\n257\t\n258\t(defn- ordered\n259\t  \"`coll` in the order the export walks it: by the canonical bytes of\n260\t   `(keyfn x)`'s encoding under a version-1 export, so cell numbering\n261\t   never depends on a host's map or set iteration; as given under\n262\t   version 0, whose wire is frozen.\"\n263\t  [found keyfn coll]\n264\t  (if-some [order (:order @found)]\n265\t    (order keyfn coll)\n266\t    coll))\n267\t\n268\t\n269\t(declare value-encoder registers-v2)\n270\t\n271\t\n272\t(defn- canonical-order\n273\t  \"The ordering function of a version-1 export: `(order keyfn coll)`\n274\t   sorts `coll` by the canonical bytes of the scratch encoding of each\n275\t   `(keyfn x)`.  The scratch encoder owns a found map of its own, so it\n276\t   mints nothing the export keeps; it runs under `:ordering`, so every\n277\t   cell its keys meet is seeded by the identity the cell table keys by,\n278\t   never by a number a comparison could shift, and it orders its own\n279\t   nested maps the same way.  Ties keep the walk order given: wait\n280\t   order and alias identity are never reordered.\"\n281\t  [vm serve! v2]\n282\t  (let [self (volatile! nil)\n283\t        order (fn [keyfn coll]\n284\t                (sort-by (comp @self keyfn) jing.cbor/encoded-compare coll))\n285\t        encode (value-encoder vm serve!\n286\t                              (atom (cond-> (assoc (new-found)\n287\t                                                   :order order\n288\t                                                   :jing-codec true\n289\t                                                   :ordering true)\n290\t                                      v2 (assoc :v2 v2))))]\n291\t    (vreset! self encode)\n292\t    order))\n293\t\n294\t\n295\t;; =============================================================================\n296\t;; The value encoder: UCF 7.5.1 over one task's whole reachable graph\n297\t;; =============================================================================\n298\t\n299\t(defn- encode-primitive\n300\t  \"A host function as UCF 7.5.2's primitive marker: its one name in\n301\t   `vm`'s primitives, with that name's profile.  Unnamed, ambiguous\n302\t   and host-state functions are not portable.\"\n303\t  [vm f]\n304\t  (let [n (vm/name-of (:primitives vm)\n305\t                      (or (:primitive-canonical-names vm) {}) f)\n306\t        profile (when (symbol? n)\n307\t                  (vm/profile-of (:primitives vm) n))]\n308\t    (cond\n309\t      (nil? n) (non-portable! :unnamed-function {})\n310\t      (not (symbol? n)) (non-portable! :ambiguous-primitive {})\n311\t      (= :host (:yin.k/class profile))\n312\t      (non-portable! :host-state-primitive {:yin.k/name n})\n313\t      :else {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/primitive\n314\t             :yin.k/name n\n315\t             :yin.k/profile (:yin.k/profile profile)})))\n316\t\n317\t\n318\t(defn- value-encoder\n319\t  \"The encode half, over `vm`'s coordinates with the export's ONE\n320\t   found map: closures lift through the kernel (recording their origin\n321\t   segment and module store), a stream or cursor reference is\n322\t   authenticated under the source's own secret before it is encoded --\n323\t   a forged reference refuses with its kind -- and every literal map is\n324\t   wrapped, so a program's data can never forge a marker.  A host\n325\t   object, a reified continuation and a heap cell refuse (S7.5.4).\"\n326\t  [vm serve! found]\n327\t  (letfn [(encode\n328\t            [x]\n329\t            (cond\n330\t              (scalar? x) x\n331\t              ;; the canonical codec's numeric carriers (Float64, Decimal,\n332\t              ;; Rational and the like, none of them `number?` on every\n333\t              ;; host) are version-1 content: the jing body carries them\n334\t              ;; as-is, and the stream codec's frozen version-0 domain --\n335\t              ;; `portable-value?` -- does not admit them\n336\t              (jing.cbor/numeric? x)\n337\t              (if (:jing-codec @found)\n338\t                x\n339\t                (non-portable! :host-object\n340\t                               {:yin.k/hint\n341\t                                #?(:cljd (str (.-runtimeType x))\n342\t                                   :default (str (type x)))}))\n343\t              (values/host-typed? x)\n344\t              (cond\n345\t                (not (values/owned-by? x (:owner vm)))\n346\t                (non-portable! :foreign-value {:yin.k/hint (values/kind-of x)})\n347\t                (values/closure? x)\n348\t                (let [marker (module/lift-closure vm (values/payload x)\n349\t                                                  encode)]\n350\t                  (swap! found\n351\t                         (fn [acc]\n352\t                           (let [acc (-> acc\n353\t                                         (update :bound (fnil into #{})\n354\t                                                 (keys (:yin.k/env marker)))\n355\t                                         (update :segments\n356\t                                                 conj (:yin.k/segment marker)))]\n357\t                             (if-some [m (:yin.k/store-of marker)]\n358\t                               (update acc :stores conj m)\n359\t                               acc))))\n360\t                  marker)\n361\t                (and (:v2 @found) (values/continuation? x))\n362\t                {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/frame\n363\t                 :yin.k/registers (registers-v2 (:engine (:v2 @found))\n364\t                                                found encode vm\n365\t                                                (values/payload x))}\n366\t                :else\n367\t                (non-portable! :non-canonicalizable\n368\t                               {:yin.k/hint :reified-continuation}))\n369\t              (map? x)\n370\t              (case (:type x)\n371\t                :stream-ref\n372\t                (if (engine/authentic-ref? vm :stream-ref x)\n373\t                  (marker-for! vm serve! found (:id x))\n374\t                  (non-portable! :forged-resource-reference\n375\t                                 {:yin.k/hint :stream-ref}))\n376\t                :cursor-ref\n377\t                (if (engine/authentic-ref? vm :cursor-ref x)\n378\t                  {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/cursor-ref\n379\t                   :yin.k/cell (cell-for! vm serve! found (:id x))}\n380\t                  (non-portable! :forged-resource-reference\n381\t                                 {:yin.k/hint :cursor-ref}))\n382\t                :parked-continuation\n383\t                (if (:v2 @found)\n384\t                  (do (swap! found update :parked-refs (fnil conj #{}) (:id x))\n385\t                      {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/frame\n386\t                       :yin.k/parked-id (:id x)})\n387\t                  (non-portable! :non-canonicalizable\n388\t                                 {:yin.k/hint (:type x)}))\n389\t                :cell-ref\n390\t                (non-portable! :cell {:yin.k/hint (:id x)})\n391\t                {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/literal\n392\t                 :yin.k/entries\n393\t                 (into []\n394\t                       (mapcat (fn [[k v]] [(encode k) (encode v)]))\n395\t                       (ordered found key x))})\n396\t              (vector? x) (mapv encode x)\n397\t              (set? x) (into #{} (map encode) (ordered found identity x))\n398\t              (seq? x) (apply list (map encode x))\n399\t              (fn? x) (encode-primitive vm x)\n400\t              :else (non-portable! :host-object\n401\t                                   {:yin.k/hint\n402\t                                    #?(:cljd (str (.-runtimeType x))\n403\t                                       :default (str (type x)))})))]\n404\t    encode))\n405\t\n406\t\n407\t;; =============================================================================\n408\t;; Registers: the frame slice, structurally\n409\t;; =============================================================================\n410\t\n411\t(defn- seg-address!\n412\t  \"The content address of local segment id `seg`, recorded as a\n413\t   requirement of the body.  A segment with no address names nothing\n414\t   portable.\"\n415\t  [found vm seg]\n416\t  (if-some [a (get-in vm [:code seg :address])]\n417\t    (do (swap! found update :segments conj a) a)\n418\t    (non-portable! :unaddressed-segment {:yin.k/hint seg})))\n419\t\n420\t\n421\t(defn- encode-env\n422\t  \"One environment: keys as carried (names), values encoded, and the\n423\t   active module store it names -- when it names one -- recorded as a\n424\t   store the body must snapshot.\"\n425\t  [found encode env]\n426\t  (when-some [m (get env engine/store-of-key)]\n427\t    (swap! found update :stores conj m))\n428\t  (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (encode v)])) (ordered found key env)))\n429\t\n430\t\n431\t(defn- encode-frame\n432\t  \"One K frame: its own keys, the segment as its address, the\n433\t   environment encoded as one.\"\n434\t  [found encode vm frame]\n435\t  (into {}\n436\t        (map (fn [[k v]]\n437\t               [k (cond\n438\t                    (= :segment k) (seg-address! found vm v)\n439\t                    (= :env k) (encode-env found encode v)\n440\t                    :else (encode v))]))\n441\t        (ordered found key frame)))\n442\t\n443\t\n444\t(defn- encode-registers\n445\t  \"One register map -- a wait entry's or a parked record's frame slice\n446\t   -- without its transport fields: they travel as the pending.\"\n447\t  [found encode vm {:keys [segment pc env stack k]}]\n448\t  (cond-> {:yin.k/pc pc\n449\t           :yin.k/env (encode-env found encode (or env {}))\n450\t           :yin.k/stack (mapv encode (or stack []))\n451\t           :yin.k/k (mapv (partial encode-frame found encode vm)\n452\t                          (or k []))}\n453\t    (some? segment)\n454\t    (assoc :yin.k/segment (seg-address! found vm segment))))\n455\t\n456\t\n457\t(defn- decode-env\n458\t  [decode env]\n459\t  (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (decode v)])) env))\n460\t\n461\t\n462\t(defn- decode-frame\n463\t  [decode aliases frame]\n464\t  (into {}\n465\t        (map (fn [[k v]]\n466\t               [k (cond\n467\t                    (= :segment k) (get aliases v)\n468\t                    (= :env k) (decode-env decode v)\n469\t                    :else (decode v))]))\n470\t        frame))\n471\t\n472\t\n473\t(defn- decode-registers\n474\t  \"The register map back in the receiver's coordinates: segments\n475\t   through the alias column of the attached code, values decoded and\n476\t   re-sealed under the receiving task.\"\n477\t  [decode aliases r]\n478\t  (cond-> {:pc (:yin.k/pc r)\n479\t           :env (decode-env decode (:yin.k/env r))\n480\t           :stack (mapv decode (:yin.k/stack r))\n481\t           :k (mapv (partial decode-frame decode aliases)\n482\t                    (or (:yin.k/k r) []))}\n483\t    (some? (:yin.k/segment r))\n484\t    (assoc :segment (get aliases (:yin.k/segment r)))))\n485\t\n486\t\n487\t;; =============================================================================\n488\t;; Dynamic reasons: observed evidence against the static kinds\n489\t;; =============================================================================\n490\t\n491\t(def ^:private wire-of-kind\n492\t  \"The wire variants each static safepoint kind admits.  The static map\n493\t   says where an instruction may park; the observed entry says why this\n494\t   activation did.  An explicit park admits no waiter at all, and an\n495\t   `:effectful-call` admits whatever effect the activation actually\n496\t   produced -- a read, a write, an FFI state or a link state -- because\n497\t   the instruction's kind selects none of them.\"\n498\t  {:explicit-park #{}\n499\t   :blocked-read #{:next}\n500\t   :blocked-write #{:put}\n501\t   :ffi-sent #{:ffi}\n502\t   :ffi-retained #{:ffi-request}\n503\t   :effectful-call #{:next :put :ffi :ffi-request\n504\t                     :link-request :link-response :install}})\n505\t\n506\t\n507\t(declare observed-wire* row-children)\n508\t\n509\t\n510\t(defn- walker-ffi-frame\n511\t  \"The FFI wrapper frame the walker entry `entry` rides on top of, or\n512\t   nil: a response reader's `eval-call` carrying its call id, or a\n513\t   retained request's `request-sent`.\"\n514\t  [entry]\n515\t  (let [k (:k entry)]\n516\t    (case (:type k)\n517\t      :dao.stream.apply/eval-call (when (contains? k :call-id) k)\n518\t      :dao.stream.apply/request-sent k\n519\t      nil)))\n520\t\n521\t\n522\t(defn- entry-call-id\n523\t  \"The FFI call id of `entry`: its own under the positional and\n524\t   semantic profiles, the wrapper frame's under the walker.\"\n525\t  [engine entry]\n526\t  (if (= :walker engine)\n527\t    (let [k (walker-ffi-frame entry)]\n528\t      (or (:call-id k) (:parked-id k)))\n529\t    (:call-id entry)))\n530\t\n531\t\n532\t(defn- observed-wire\n533\t  \"The wire variant the observed entry itself carries, from its shape\n534\t   alone: a `:next` wait with a call id is a sent FFI response reader;\n535\t   a `:put` wait holding its request is a retained call.  The walker\n536\t   carries that identity in its wrapper frame.  nil when the entry is no\n537\t   variant at all.\"\n538\t  ([entry] (observed-wire entry nil))\n539\t  ([entry engine]\n540\t   (if (= :walker engine)\n541\t     (case (:reason entry)\n542\t       :next (if (= :dao.stream.apply/eval-call (:type (walker-ffi-frame entry)))\n543\t               :ffi :next)\n544\t       :put (if (= :dao.stream.apply/request-sent\n545\t                   (:type (walker-ffi-frame entry)))\n546\t              :ffi-request :put)\n547\t       (observed-wire entry nil))\n548\t     (observed-wire* entry))))\n549\t\n550\t\n551\t(defn- observed-wire*\n552\t  [entry]\n553\t  (case (:reason entry)\n554\t    :next (if (:call-id entry) :ffi :next)\n555\t    :put (if (:request-sent entry) :ffi-request :put)\n556\t    :link-request :link-request\n557\t    :link-response :link-response\n558\t    :install :install\n559\t    nil))\n560\t\n561\t\n562\t(defn- safepoint-kinds-at\n563\t  \"The static `:yin.safepoint/kinds` at the resume pc of `seg`, from\n564\t   the loaded image's own canonical vector; an undeclared pc refuses\n565\t   with the existing :yin.k/not-at-safepoint outcome.\"\n566\t  [vm seg pc]\n567\t  (let [image (get (:code vm) seg)\n568\t        v (when image (completion/image->vector image))]\n569\t    (cond\n570\t      (nil? image) (non-portable! :unaddressed-segment {:yin.k/hint seg})\n571\t      (nil? v) (non-portable! :address-mismatch {:yin.k/hint seg})\n572\t      :else\n573\t      (let [at (ucf/safepoint-at v pc)]\n574\t        (if (contains? at :yin.k/status)\n575\t          (not-at-safepoint! pc)\n576\t          (:yin.safepoint/kinds at))))))\n577\t\n578\t\n579\t;; =============================================================================\n580\t;; What cannot lift at all (UCF 7.4.1, 7.4.3): holds with no wire form\n581\t;; =============================================================================\n582\t\n583\t(defn- held?\n584\t  [x]\n585\t  (and (map? x) (contains? x :yin.k/held)))\n586\t\n587\t\n588\t(defn- unliftable-hold\n589\t  \"The first thing `vm` holds that has no wire pending variant at any\n590\t   version, as the data the refusal carries, or nil: a held observation\n591\t   -- an `:observe` entry, or an entry or cursor cell carrying\n592\t   `:yin.k/held` --, a reachable unminted cursor cell, a pending close,\n593\t   or a `:link-request` entry whose response cursor is not installed.\n594\t   Entering exporting refuses the same holds over the whole task (D8);\n595\t   the lift refuses them here, before `lift-pending!`, so its\n596\t   undecodable fall-through is never reached for these, in the root and\n597\t   in every install child through the recursive export.\"\n598\t  [vm]\n599\t  (let [waits (:wait-set vm)\n600\t        cells (filter map? (vals (:resources vm)))]\n601\t    (cond\n602\t      (some #(= :observe (:reason %)) waits)\n603\t      {:yin.k/hold :observe}\n604\t\n605\t      (or (some held? waits) (some held? cells))\n606\t      {:yin.k/hold :held}\n607\t\n608\t      (some :yin.k/unminted cells)\n609\t      {:yin.k/hold :unminted-cursor}\n610\t\n611\t      (seq (:yin.k/closes vm))\n612\t      {:yin.k/hold :pending-close}\n613\t\n614\t      (some #(and (= :link-request (:reason %)) (not (contains? % :cursor)))\n615\t            waits)\n616\t      {:yin.k/hold :link-cursor-not-installed})))\n617\t\n618\t\n619\t;; =============================================================================\n620\t;; Protection (UCF 7.4.3, 7.7.8): the operation id against the enrolled set\n621\t;; =============================================================================\n622\t\n623\t(defn- protected!\n624\t  \"`pending` under a version-1 export's protection rules.  A retained\n625\t   `:put`, `:ffi-request` or `:link-request` entry whose target is in\n626\t   the header's enrolled set must carry an operation id -- one attempted\n627\t   without it cannot be made exactly-once afterwards, so the lift\n628\t   refuses `:unprotected-pending` -- and an entry carrying an id whose\n629\t   target is not enrolled is unsatisfied, naming the stream: protection\n630\t   is neither added to an attempted write nor dropped from one.  The id\n631\t   is the entry's `:op-id`, copied to `:yin.k/op-id`.  Version 0 names\n632\t   no custody and returns `pending` as it was.\"\n633\t  [found entry pending]\n634\t  (let [reason (:yin.k/reason pending)]\n635\t    (if-not (and (:jing-codec @found)\n636\t                 (contains? #{:put :ffi-request :link-request} reason))\n637\t      pending\n638\t      (let [target (:dao.stream/identity\n639\t                     (get pending (if (= :put reason)\n640\t                                    :yin.k/stream\n641\t                                    :yin.k/request)))\n642\t            enrolled? (contains? (:enrolled @found) target)\n643\t            carried? (some? (:op-id entry))]\n644\t        (cond\n645\t          (and enrolled? (not carried?))\n646\t          (non-portable! :unprotected-pending {:dao.stream/identity target})\n647\t\n648\t          (and carried? (not enrolled?))\n649\t          (unsatisfied! target)\n650\t\n651\t          carried?\n652\t          (assoc pending :yin.k/op-id (:op-id entry))\n653\t\n654\t          :else pending)))))\n655\t\n656\t\n657\t;; =============================================================================\n658\t;; Lift: one pending variant each, from the observed entry\n659\t;; =============================================================================\n660\t\n661\t(defn- call-out-cell\n662\t  \"The emitter's call-out cursor cell -- the response route a retained\n663\t   call held.  nil when the composition holds no call pair, which no\n664\t   real retained request does.\"\n665\t  [resources]\n666\t  (let [cursor (get resources vm/call-out-cursor-key)\n667\t        handle (get resources vm/call-out-stream-key)]\n668\t    (when (and (map? cursor) (contains? cursor :stream-id) handle)\n669\t      {:id vm/call-out-cursor-key\n670\t       :stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key\n671\t       :cursor (:cursor cursor)})))\n672\t\n673\t\n674\t(defn- lift-pending!\n675\t  \"The S7.4.3 pending of one observed entry, in `yin.vm.ucf.remote`'s\n676\t   wire shapes, minted through THIS export's one cell and marker maps:\n677\t   the cell a waiter names is the same cell a closure or the store\n678\t   reaches, and the response route a retained call held is a cell like\n679\t   any other, at its kept position.\"\n680\t  [vm serve! found encode entry]\n681\t  (case (observed-wire entry (:engine (:v2 @found)))\n682\t    :next\n683\t    {:yin.k/reason :next\n684\t     :yin.k/cell (cell-for! vm serve! found\n685\t                            (get-in entry [:cursor-ref :id]))}\n686\t\n687\t    :ffi\n688\t    (cond-> {:yin.k/reason :ffi\n689\t             :yin.k/call-id (entry-call-id (:engine (:v2 @found)) entry)\n690\t             :yin.k/cell (cell-for! vm serve! found\n691\t                                    (get-in entry [:cursor-ref :id]))}\n692\t      (contains? entry :op) (assoc :yin.k/op (:op entry)))\n693\t\n694\t    :put\n695\t    (do (when-not (contains? entry :datom)\n696\t          (non-portable! :incomplete-write\n697\t                         {:yin.k/pc (:pc entry)}))\n698\t        {:yin.k/reason :put\n699\t         :yin.k/stream (marker-for! vm serve! found (:stream-id entry))\n700\t         :yin.k/value (encode (:datom entry))})\n701\t\n702\t    :ffi-request\n703\t    (let [route (if (and (:response-cursor entry)\n704\t                         (:response-stream entry)\n705\t                         (:yin.k/recovery-cell-ids vm))\n706\t                  {:id (:response-cursor entry)\n707\t                   :stream-id (:response-stream entry)}\n708\t                  (call-out-cell (:resources vm)))]\n709\t      (if (nil? route)\n710\t        (unsatisfied!)\n711\t        (let [envelope (:datom entry)]\n712\t          {:yin.k/reason :ffi-request\n713\t           :yin.k/call-id (entry-call-id (:engine (:v2 @found)) entry)\n714\t           :yin.k/request-envelope (encode envelope)\n715\t           :yin.k/request-op (or (apply2/request-op envelope)\n716\t                                 (:op entry)\n717\t                                 (:op (:k entry)))\n718\t           :yin.k/request-args (apply2/request-args envelope)\n719\t           :yin.k/request (marker-for! vm serve! found\n720\t                                       (:stream-id entry))\n721\t           :yin.k/response (marker-for! vm serve! found\n722\t                                        (:stream-id route))\n723\t           :yin.k/response-cell (cell-for! vm serve! found\n724\t                                           (:id route))})))\n725\t\n726\t    (:link-request :link-response)\n727\t    (let [reason (:reason entry)\n728\t          kept (:cursor entry)]\n729\t      (cond-> {:yin.k/reason reason\n730\t               :yin.k/link-id (:link-id entry)\n731\t               :yin.k/name (:name entry)\n732\t               :yin.k/request (marker-for! vm serve! found\n733\t                                           (:request entry))\n734\t               :yin.k/response (marker-for! vm serve! found\n735\t                                            (:response entry))\n736\t               :yin.k/cell (cell-at! vm serve! found\n737\t                                     [(:response entry) kept]\n738\t                                     (:response entry) kept)}\n739\t        (= :link-request reason)\n740\t        (assoc :yin.k/envelope (encode (:envelope entry)))))\n741\t\n742\t    :install\n743\t    (do (when-not (contains? (:installs vm) (:name entry))\n744\t          (non-portable! :incomplete-install {:yin.k/name (:name entry)}))\n745\t        {:yin.k/reason :install\n746\t         :yin.k/name (:name entry)})\n747\t\n748\t    (undecodable! {:yin.k/reason (:reason entry)\n749\t                   :yin.k/path [:yin.k/wait (:pc entry)]})))\n750\t\n751\t\n752\t(declare pc-profile? site-op site-reasons module-decls)\n753\t\n754\t\n755\t(defn- lift-frame!\n756\t  \"One wait entry lifted: its registers and its pending, the dynamic\n757\t   reason checked against the static kinds at its pc -- the kinds gate\n758\t   eligibility only, and a variant they do not admit is evidence the\n759\t   frame is not exportable here, never a wire reason to invent.\"\n760\t  [vm serve! found encode entry]\n761\t  (let [engine (:engine (:v2 @found))\n762\t        pc? (pc-profile? engine)\n763\t        walker? (= :walker engine)\n764\t        kinds (when-not (or pc? walker?)\n765\t                (safepoint-kinds-at vm (:segment entry) (:pc entry)))\n766\t        wire (observed-wire entry engine)]\n767\t    (when (nil? wire)\n768\t      (undecodable! {:yin.k/reason (:reason entry)\n769\t                     :yin.k/path [:yin.k/wait (:pc entry)]}))\n770\t    (when-not (cond\n771\t                walker? true\n772\t                pc? (contains? (get site-reasons (site-op engine entry)) wire)\n773\t                :else (some #(contains? (get wire-of-kind %) wire) kinds))\n774\t      (non-portable! :reason-mismatch\n775\t                     {:yin.k/pc (:pc entry)\n776\t                      :yin.k/reason wire\n777\t                      :yin.safepoint/kinds (vec kinds)}))\n778\t    {:yin.k/registers (if-some [v2 (:v2 @found)]\n779\t                        (registers-v2 (:engine v2) found encode vm entry)\n780\t                        (encode-registers found encode vm entry))\n781\t     :yin.k/pending (protected! found entry\n782\t                                (lift-pending! vm serve! found encode\n783\t                                               entry))}))\n784\t\n785\t\n786\t;; =============================================================================\n787\t;; The install children: a whole child travels, or nothing does\n788\t;; =============================================================================\n789\t\n790\t(declare export-task validate-body validate-body-v1 validate-body-v2\n791\t         v2-body? resume-task resume-task*)\n792\t\n793\t\n794\t(defn- portable-response?\n795\t  \"True when install `response` survives the body's own codec.\"\n796\t  [jing-codec? response]\n797\t  (if jing-codec?\n798\t    (try (jing.cbor/encode response) true\n799\t         (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ false))\n800\t    (cbor/portable-value? response)))\n801\t\n802\t\n803\t(defn- export-installs\n804\t  \"Each live install child of `vm` as its own handoff body beside the\n805\t   response that spawned it, preserving the child's phase and waits\n806\t   (14.1.1's :install row).  A child that cannot export itself refuses\n807\t   the parent's export -- a refusal is thrown, never embedded -- and a\n808\t   response outside the canonical bytes domain refuses it too.  Under\n809\t   version 1 the child is a part of its root's task: it carries the\n810\t   root's version and enrolled set, no header, and its phase, a wire\n811\t   phase (`:running` or `:parked`), and parent always travel.\"\n812\t  [vm serve! opts]\n813\t  (let [jing-codec? (::jing-codec opts)]\n814\t    (into {}\n815\t          (map (fn [[m {:keys [vm phase parent response]}]]\n816\t                 (when-not (portable-response? jing-codec? response)\n817\t                   (non-portable! :install-response {:yin.k/name m}))\n818\t                 (when (and jing-codec? (not (contains? #{:running :parked} phase)))\n819\t                   (non-portable! :incomplete-install\n820\t                                  {:yin.k/name m :yin.k/phase phase}))\n821\t                 (let [r (export-task vm serve!\n822\t                                      (assoc opts\n823\t                                             :path (conj (:path opts) m)\n824\t                                             ::child true))]\n825\t                   (when (not= :ok (:status r))\n826\t                     (refuse! (:yin.k/status r) (dissoc r :status)))\n827\t                   [m {:yin.k/phase phase\n828\t                       :yin.k/parent parent\n829\t                       :yin.k/response response\n830\t                       :yin.k/child (:body r)}])))\n831\t          (:installs vm))))\n832\t\n833\t\n834\t;; =============================================================================\n835\t;; Version 2 lift: one adapter per execution profile (UCF v2 amendment)\n836\t;; =============================================================================\n837\t\n838\t(defn- engine-of\n839\t  \"The version-2 engine of `vm`, from the kernel's own link format: the\n840\t   profile is the kernel's, never inferred from an image's shape.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee657710-cc1c-4c43-882b-5874c9a79051","uuid":"3c82c2bf-126b-46ef-a436-76a5d4a5198e","timestamp":"2026-10-12T15:53:06.992Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6b/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.handoff\n  \"Stage 1 of the post-M5 hardening (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md\n   section 14.1): the kept-cursor handoff -- one blocked or halted task\n   exported as canonical bytes, resumed as a fresh task on another host.\n\n   `export-task` is the lift of 14.1.2: it validates the safepoint and\n   the empty ready queue, captures the ordered waits without polling\n   them, walks the reachable graph with ONE source-resource-to-cell\n   map (`yin.vm.completion`'s fixed point over the whole frame set, so\n   two waiters on one cell lift to one UCF cell and a cell a closure or\n   the store also reaches shares the same id), derives every dynamic\n   reason and pending variant from the OBSERVED wait entry -- never\n   from the static `:yin.safepoint/kinds` at the pc, which only gates\n   eligibility (`yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md` section 8) -- closes the\n   requirements, validates the whole body, and answers it as canonical\n   CBOR bytes under their content address.\n\n   `resume-task` is the lower, and its reader is version-aware (M-next\n   D7): the version-1 decode is tried first -- `dao.jing.cbor` canonical\n   bytes, whose decoder refuses the stream codec's tag-39 identifiers --\n   then the stage-1 `dao.stream.cbor` decode; the codec that accepted\n   the bytes decides which body version they may carry (version 1 in\n   jing bytes, version 0 in stream bytes, enforced as\n   `:yin.k/profile-mismatch` before the address check), a version-1\n   body then runs the custody inspector (`yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint`) over\n   its claimed address, and a failure at any step is never\n   reinterpreted through the other codec.  It checks stamp, grammar,\n   references and code hashes before anything is installed;\n   attach each stream identity once through its carried descriptor;\n   allocate one fresh private resource per logical cell and stream;\n   re-seal every reference under the receiving task; restore the store\n   slice, the module stores, the counter and the parked records, then\n   the ordered waits; and answer the runnable machine only after all\n   restoration passes.  A failed lower installs nothing partially\n   runnable: refusals are total.\n\n   The transfer seam is the same composition pair `yin.vm.ucf.remote`\n   defined: `serve!` (the exporter's remote-table entry, so the source\n   keeps serving the stream) and `attach!` (the receiver's dispatch).\n   Version 0 resumes as a fork. Version 1 restores a running root only\n   with composition-supplied grant evidence and protection declarations;\n   halted results restore ended, and install children carry the gate only.\n\n   Halt is a result, never a frame: the halted body carries the result\n   and no wait at all.  An explicit park is the no-wait shape: the\n   parked record travels in the scheduler slice under its own id and\n   no pending is minted for it.  An install waiter travels beside its\n   whole child -- the child's own handoff body, phase and response --\n   or the export refuses; an install name alone reconstructs nothing.\"\n  (:require [clojure.set :as set]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as jing.cbor]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n            [dao.stream.cbor :as cbor]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as walker]\n            [yin.vm.completion :as completion]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-effects :as reffects]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as register]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as stack]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.integer.host :as integer-host]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.ucf :as ucf]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint :as checkpoint]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.custody :as custody]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.remote :as ucf.remote]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n\n\n(def handoff-tag\n  \"The S7.5.1 tag of one handoff body.\"\n  :yin.k/handoff)\n\n\n(def handoff-version\n  \"The body versions this namespace's reader speaks: version 0, the\n   frozen stage-1 wire the lower still emits, version 1, the custody\n   amendment (section 14.3) whose canonical bytes are dao.jing.cbor's,\n   and version 2, the four-profile amendment\n   (docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md),\n   also in dao.jing.cbor bytes.  Which a body may carry is decided by\n   the codec that accepted its bytes -- the version-aware reader's gate,\n   before the tag grammar and before any address or restoration check --\n   and a body of any other version, absent or not of the integer kind,\n   is refused with :yin.k/profile-mismatch.  Version 2 is dispatched\n   by exact integer kind and structural role, never by `>= 1`: it is\n   selected at export by the composition's `:version 2` option.\"\n  #{0 1 2})\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Refusal vocabulary (S7.9): every failure is a data outcome\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- refuse!\n  [status data]\n  (throw (ex-info (str \"Handoff refused: \" (name status))\n                  (merge {:yin.k/status status} data))))\n\n\n(defn- non-portable!\n  [kind data]\n  (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable (assoc data :yin.k/kind kind)))\n\n\n(defn- unsatisfied!\n  ([] (unsatisfied! nil))\n  ([identity]\n   (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied\n            (cond-> {} (some? identity)\n                    (assoc :dao.stream/identity identity)))))\n\n\n(defn- undecodable!\n  [data]\n  (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable data))\n\n\n(defn- not-at-safepoint!\n  [pc]\n  (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint {:yin.k/pc pc}))\n\n\n(defn- outcome\n  \"The S7.9 data outcome exception `e` carries, or nil.\"\n  [e]\n  (let [d (ex-data e)]\n    (when (and (map? d) (contains? d :yin.k/status)) d)))\n\n\n(defn- call!\n  \"Run `f`, answering its value, or the data outcome it refused with.\n   A throw with no outcome vocabulary is a defect, not a refusal: it\n   propagates.\"\n  [f]\n  (try (f)\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n         (if-let [d (outcome e)] d (throw e)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The one cell map (14.1.2 lift step 2): minted across the WHOLE set\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- scalar?\n  [x]\n  (or (nil? x) (boolean? x)\n      (and (number? x) (not (integer-host/big-carrier? x)))\n      (string? x) (keyword? x) (symbol? x)))\n\n\n(defn- local-identity\n  \"The identity `h` itself declares, when its descriptor answers ok;\n   nil otherwise -- the best name a refusal can give before `serve!`.\"\n  [h]\n  (let [d (when (stream/descriptor? h) (stream/descriptor h))]\n    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome d))\n      (:dao.stream/identity d))))\n\n\n(defn- marker-for!\n  \"The UCF stream marker for the stream resource `id` of `vm`, minted\n   through the exporter's own table (`serve!`) once per resource: the\n   descriptor serve! answers, never a handle.  A resource id the\n   private table does not hold is a forged reference; `serve!` here is\n   the keyed form `(serve! id handle)` of `export-task`, so the answer\n   is retained under the resource id, never under the handle.  A stream the\n   table cannot serve is unsatisfied, naming the identity where one is\n   known.  Two resources of one identity mint two markers that name\n   the one identity -- the lower attaches per identity, once.  Under\n   the ordering scratch the marker is seeded by the resource id and\n   nothing is asked: a sort comparison serves no stream and mints no\n   identity, exactly as it mints no cell number.\"\n  [vm serve! found id]\n  (if (:ordering @found)\n    (or (get-in @found [:markers id])\n        (let [m {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/stream\n                 :dao.stream/identity id\n                 :dao.stream/descriptor {:yin.k/hint :ordering}}]\n          (swap! found assoc-in [:markers id] m)\n          m))\n    (let [handle (get (:resources vm) id)]\n      (if (nil? handle)\n        (non-portable! :forged-resource-reference {:yin.k/hint id})\n        (or (get-in @found [:markers id])\n            (if-let [marker (ucf.remote/lift-marker (partial serve! id)\n                                                    handle)]\n              (do (swap! found assoc-in [:markers id] marker) marker)\n              (unsatisfied! (local-identity handle))))))))\n\n\n(defn- portable-cursor\n  \"The kept cursor when it survives a round trip through the body's\n   own canonical codec -- encoded, decoded back, equal -- which is what\n   the :dao.stream.remote/v1 claim means for this body.  nil when it\n   does not, so no cell is ever published over an unpublishable\n   cursor.\"\n  [kept]\n  (try (let [b (cbor/encode kept)]\n         (when (= kept (cbor/decode b)) kept))\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n\n\n(defn- cell-at!\n  \"The logical cursor cell for an explicit kept position on the stream\n   resource `stream-id` (UCF 7.5.3), minted once per `key` across the\n   WHOLE export: two references through one key share one cell id.\n   Cell ids are lift-local identities, never content or position\n   hashes.  Under the ordering scratch (`:ordering`) the id IS the key\n   -- the resource id, or the position pair, the very identity the cell\n   table itself keys by -- so a sort comparison never mints a number\n   and no traversal order can change which distinct cursor sorts\n   first.\"\n  [vm serve! found key stream-id kept]\n  (or (get-in @found [:cell-of key])\n      (let [marker (marker-for! vm serve! found stream-id)]\n        (if (some? (portable-cursor kept))\n          (let [cid (if (:ordering @found)\n                      key\n                      (or (get-in @found [:recovery-cell-ids key])\n                          (keyword \"yin.k\" (str \"c-\" (count (:cells @found))))))]\n            (swap! found\n                   (fn [acc]\n                     (-> acc\n                         (assoc-in [:cell-of key] cid)\n                         (assoc-in [:cells cid]\n                                   {:yin.k/stream marker\n                                    :yin.k/position kept}))))\n            cid)\n          (unsatisfied! (:dao.stream/identity marker))))))\n\n\n(defn- cell-for!\n  \"The cell the cursor-cell resource `id` lifts to: the entry's kept\n   position on its own stream.  A key naming no resource is a forged\n   reference.\"\n  [vm serve! found id]\n  (let [cell (get (:resources vm) id)]\n    (if (nil? cell)\n      (non-portable! :forged-resource-reference {:yin.k/hint id})\n      (cell-at! vm serve! found id (:stream-id cell) (:cursor cell)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The found map and the canonical order of a version-1 export\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- new-found\n  []\n  {:cells {} :cell-of {} :markers {} :stores #{} :segments #{}})\n\n\n(defn- ordered\n  \"`coll` in the order the export walks it: by the canonical bytes of\n   `(keyfn x)`'s encoding under a version-1 export, so cell numbering\n   never depends on a host's map or set iteration; as given under\n   version 0, whose wire is frozen.\"\n  [found keyfn coll]\n  (if-some [order (:order @found)]\n    (order keyfn coll)\n    coll))\n\n\n(declare value-encoder registers-v2)\n\n\n(defn- canonical-order\n  \"The ordering function of a version-1 export: `(order keyfn coll)`\n   sorts `coll` by the canonical bytes of the scratch encoding of each\n   `(keyfn x)`.  The scratch encoder owns a found map of its own, so it\n   mints nothing the export keeps; it runs under `:ordering`, so every\n   cell its keys meet is seeded by the identity the cell table keys by,\n   never by a number a comparison could shift, and it orders its own\n   nested maps the same way.  Ties keep the walk order given: wait\n   order and alias identity are never reordered.\"\n  [vm serve! v2]\n  (let [self (volatile! nil)\n        order (fn [keyfn coll]\n                (sort-by (comp @self keyfn) jing.cbor/encoded-compare coll))\n        encode (value-encoder vm serve!\n                              (atom (cond-> (assoc (new-found)\n                                                   :order order\n                                                   :jing-codec true\n                                                   :ordering true)\n                                      v2 (assoc :v2 v2))))]\n    (vreset! self encode)\n    order))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The value encoder: UCF 7.5.1 over one task's whole reachable graph\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- encode-primitive\n  \"A host function as UCF 7.5.2's primitive marker: its one name in\n   `vm`'s primitives, with that name's profile.  Unnamed, ambiguous\n   and host-state functions are not portable.\"\n  [vm f]\n  (let [n (vm/name-of (:primitives vm)\n                      (or (:primitive-canonical-names vm) {}) f)\n        profile (when (symbol? n)\n                  (vm/profile-of (:primitives vm) n))]\n    (cond\n      (nil? n) (non-portable! :unnamed-function {})\n      (not (symbol? n)) (non-portable! :ambiguous-primitive {})\n      (= :host (:yin.k/class profile))\n      (non-portable! :host-state-primitive {:yin.k/name n})\n      :else {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/primitive\n             :yin.k/name n\n             :yin.k/profile (:yin.k/profile profile)})))\n\n\n(defn- value-encoder\n  \"The encode half, over `vm`'s coordinates with the export's ONE\n   found map: closures lift through the kernel (recording their origin\n   segment and module store), a stream or cursor reference is\n   authenticated under the source's own secret before it is encoded --\n   a forged reference refuses with its kind -- and every literal map is\n   wrapped, so a program's data can never forge a marker.  A host\n   object, a reified continuation and a heap cell refuse (S7.5.4).\"\n  [vm serve! found]\n  (letfn [(encode\n            [x]\n            (cond\n              (scalar? x) x\n              ;; the canonical codec's numeric carriers (Float64, Decimal,\n              ;; Rational and the like, none of them `number?` on every\n              ;; host) are version-1 content: the jing body carries them\n              ;; as-is, and the stream codec's frozen version-0 domain --\n              ;; `portable-value?` -- does not admit them\n              (jing.cbor/numeric? x)\n              (if (:jing-codec @found)\n                x\n                (non-portable! :host-object\n                               {:yin.k/hint\n                                #?(:cljd (str (.-runtimeType x))\n                                   :default (str (type x)))}))\n              (values/host-typed? x)\n              (cond\n                (not (values/owned-by? x (:owner vm)))\n                (non-portable! :foreign-value {:yin.k/hint (values/kind-of x)})\n                (values/closure? x)\n                (let [marker (module/lift-closure vm (values/payload x)\n                                                  encode)]\n                  (swap! found\n                         (fn [acc]\n                           (let [acc (-> acc\n                                         (update :bound (fnil into #{})\n                                                 (keys (:yin.k/env marker)))\n                                         (update :segments\n                                                 conj (:yin.k/segment marker)))]\n                             (if-some [m (:yin.k/store-of marker)]\n                               (update acc :stores conj m)\n                               acc))))\n                  marker)\n                (and (:v2 @found) (values/continuation? x))\n                {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/frame\n                 :yin.k/registers (registers-v2 (:engine (:v2 @found))\n                                                found encode vm\n                                                (values/payload x))}\n                :else\n                (non-portable! :non-canonicalizable\n                               {:yin.k/hint :reified-continuation}))\n              (map? x)\n              (case (:type x)\n                :stream-ref\n                (if (engine/authentic-ref? vm :stream-ref x)\n                  (marker-for! vm serve! found (:id x))\n                  (non-portable! :forged-resource-reference\n                                 {:yin.k/hint :stream-ref}))\n                :cursor-ref\n                (if (engine/authentic-ref? vm :cursor-ref x)\n                  {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/cursor-ref\n                   :yin.k/cell (cell-for! vm serve! found (:id x))}\n                  (non-portable! :forged-resource-reference\n                                 {:yin.k/hint :cursor-ref}))\n                :parked-continuation\n                (if (:v2 @found)\n                  (do (swap! found update :parked-refs (fnil conj #{}) (:id x))\n                      {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/frame\n                       :yin.k/parked-id (:id x)})\n                  (non-portable! :non-canonicalizable\n                                 {:yin.k/hint (:type x)}))\n                :cell-ref\n                (non-portable! :cell {:yin.k/hint (:id x)})\n                {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/literal\n                 :yin.k/entries\n                 (into []\n                       (mapcat (fn [[k v]] [(encode k) (encode v)]))\n                       (ordered found key x))})\n              (vector? x) (mapv encode x)\n              (set? x) (into #{} (map encode) (ordered found identity x))\n              (seq? x) (apply list (map encode x))\n              (fn? x) (encode-primitive vm x)\n              :else (non-portable! :host-object\n                                   {:yin.k/hint\n                                    #?(:cljd (str (.-runtimeType x))\n                                       :default (str (type x)))})))]\n    encode))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Registers: the frame slice, structurally\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- seg-address!\n  \"The content address of local segment id `seg`, recorded as a\n   requirement of the body.  A segment with no address names nothing\n   portable.\"\n  [found vm seg]\n  (if-some [a (get-in vm [:code seg :address])]\n    (do (swap! found update :segments conj a) a)\n    (non-portable! :unaddressed-segment {:yin.k/hint seg})))\n\n\n(defn- encode-env\n  \"One environment: keys as carried (names), values encoded, and the\n   active module store it names -- when it names one -- recorded as a\n   store the body must snapshot.\"\n  [found encode env]\n  (when-some [m (get env engine/store-of-key)]\n    (swap! found update :stores conj m))\n  (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (encode v)])) (ordered found key env)))\n\n\n(defn- encode-frame\n  \"One K frame: its own keys, the segment as its address, the\n   environment encoded as one.\"\n  [found encode vm frame]\n  (into {}\n        (map (fn [[k v]]\n               [k (cond\n                    (= :segment k) (seg-address! found vm v)\n                    (= :env k) (encode-env found encode v)\n                    :else (encode v))]))\n        (ordered found key frame)))\n\n\n(defn- encode-registers\n  \"One register map -- a wait entry's or a parked record's frame slice\n   -- without its transport fields: they travel as the pending.\"\n  [found encode vm {:keys [segment pc env stack k]}]\n  (cond-> {:yin.k/pc pc\n           :yin.k/env (encode-env found encode (or env {}))\n           :yin.k/stack (mapv encode (or stack []))\n           :yin.k/k (mapv (partial encode-frame found encode vm)\n                          (or k []))}\n    (some? segment)\n    (assoc :yin.k/segment (seg-address! found vm segment))))\n\n\n(defn- decode-env\n  [decode env]\n  (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (decode v)])) env))\n\n\n(defn- decode-frame\n  [decode aliases frame]\n  (into {}\n        (map (fn [[k v]]\n               [k (cond\n                    (= :segment k) (get aliases v)\n                    (= :env k) (decode-env decode v)\n                    :else (decode v))]))\n        frame))\n\n\n(defn- decode-registers\n  \"The register map back in the receiver's coordinates: segments\n   through the alias column of the attached code, values decoded and\n   re-sealed under the receiving task.\"\n  [decode aliases r]\n  (cond-> {:pc (:yin.k/pc r)\n           :env (decode-env decode (:yin.k/env r))\n           :stack (mapv decode (:yin.k/stack r))\n           :k (mapv (partial decode-frame decode aliases)\n                    (or (:yin.k/k r) []))}\n    (some? (:yin.k/segment r))\n    (assoc :segment (get aliases (:yin.k/segment r)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Dynamic reasons: observed evidence against the static kinds\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private wire-of-kind\n  \"The wire variants each static safepoint kind admits.  The static map\n   says where an instruction may park; the observed entry says why this\n   activation did.  An explicit park admits no waiter at all, and an\n   `:effectful-call` admits whatever effect the activation actually\n   produced -- a read, a write, an FFI state or a link state -- because\n   the instruction's kind selects none of them.\"\n  {:explicit-park #{}\n   :blocked-read #{:next}\n   :blocked-write #{:put}\n   :ffi-sent #{:ffi}\n   :ffi-retained #{:ffi-request}\n   :effectful-call #{:next :put :ffi :ffi-request\n                     :link-request :link-response :install}})\n\n\n(declare observed-wire* row-children)\n\n\n(defn- walker-ffi-frame\n  \"The FFI wrapper frame the walker entry `entry` rides on top of, or\n   nil: a response reader's `eval-call` carrying its call id, or a\n   retained request's `request-sent`.\"\n  [entry]\n  (let [k (:k entry)]\n    (case (:type k)\n      :dao.stream.apply/eval-call (when (contains? k :call-id) k)\n      :dao.stream.apply/request-sent k\n      nil)))\n\n\n(defn- entry-call-id\n  \"The FFI call id of `entry`: its own under the positional and\n   semantic profiles, the wrapper frame's under the walker.\"\n  [engine entry]\n  (if (= :walker engine)\n    (let [k (walker-ffi-frame entry)]\n      (or (:call-id k) (:parked-id k)))\n    (:call-id entry)))\n\n\n(defn- observed-wire\n  \"The wire variant the observed entry itself carries, from its shape\n   alone: a `:next` wait with a call id is a sent FFI response reader;\n   a `:put` wait holding its request is a retained call.  The walker\n   carries that identity in its wrapper frame.  nil when the entry is no\n   variant at all.\"\n  ([entry] (observed-wire entry nil))\n  ([entry engine]\n   (if (= :walker engine)\n     (case (:reason entry)\n       :next (if (= :dao.stream.apply/eval-call (:type (walker-ffi-frame entry)))\n               :ffi :next)\n       :put (if (= :dao.stream.apply/request-sent\n                   (:type (walker-ffi-frame entry)))\n              :ffi-request :put)\n       (observed-wire entry nil))\n     (observed-wire* entry))))\n\n\n(defn- observed-wire*\n  [entry]\n  (case (:reason entry)\n    :next (if (:call-id entry) :ffi :next)\n    :put (if (:request-sent entry) :ffi-request :put)\n    :link-request :link-request\n    :link-response :link-response\n    :install :install\n    nil))\n\n\n(defn- safepoint-kinds-at\n  \"The static `:yin.safepoint/kinds` at the resume pc of `seg`, from\n   the loaded image's own canonical vector; an undeclared pc refuses\n   with the existing :yin.k/not-at-safepoint outcome.\"\n  [vm seg pc]\n  (let [image (get (:code vm) seg)\n        v (when image (completion/image->vector image))]\n    (cond\n      (nil? image) (non-portable! :unaddressed-segment {:yin.k/hint seg})\n      (nil? v) (non-portable! :address-mismatch {:yin.k/hint seg})\n      :else\n      (let [at (ucf/safepoint-at v pc)]\n        (if (contains? at :yin.k/status)\n          (not-at-safepoint! pc)\n          (:yin.safepoint/kinds at))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; What cannot lift at all (UCF 7.4.1, 7.4.3): holds with no wire form\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- held?\n  [x]\n  (and (map? x) (contains? x :yin.k/held)))\n\n\n(defn- unliftable-hold\n  \"The first thing `vm` holds that has no wire pending variant at any\n   version, as the data the refusal carries, or nil: a held observation\n   -- an `:observe` entry, or an entry or cursor cell carrying\n   `:yin.k/held` --, a reachable unminted cursor cell, a pending close,\n   or a `:link-request` entry whose response cursor is not installed.\n   Entering exporting refuses the same holds over the whole task (D8);\n   the lift refuses them here, before `lift-pending!`, so its\n   undecodable fall-through is never reached for these, in the root and\n   in every install child through the recursive export.\"\n  [vm]\n  (let [waits (:wait-set vm)\n        cells (filter map? (vals (:resources vm)))]\n    (cond\n      (some #(= :observe (:reason %)) waits)\n      {:yin.k/hold :observe}\n\n      (or (some held? waits) (some held? cells))\n      {:yin.k/hold :held}\n\n      (some :yin.k/unminted cells)\n      {:yin.k/hold :unminted-cursor}\n\n      (seq (:yin.k/closes vm))\n      {:yin.k/hold :pending-close}\n\n      (some #(and (= :link-request (:reason %)) (not (contains? % :cursor)))\n            waits)\n      {:yin.k/hold :link-cursor-not-installed})))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Protection (UCF 7.4.3, 7.7.8): the operation id against the enrolled set\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- protected!\n  \"`pending` under a version-1 export's protection rules.  A retained\n   `:put`, `:ffi-request` or `:link-request` entry whose target is in\n   the header's enrolled set must carry an operation id -- one attempted\n   without it cannot be made exactly-once afterwards, so the lift\n   refuses `:unprotected-pending` -- and an entry carrying an id whose\n   target is not enrolled is unsatisfied, naming the stream: protection\n   is neither added to an attempted write nor dropped from one.  The id\n   is the entry's `:op-id`, copied to `:yin.k/op-id`.  Version 0 names\n   no custody and returns `pending` as it was.\"\n  [found entry pending]\n  (let [reason (:yin.k/reason pending)]\n    (if-not (and (:jing-codec @found)\n                 (contains? #{:put :ffi-request :link-request} reason))\n      pending\n      (let [target (:dao.stream/identity\n                     (get pending (if (= :put reason)\n                                    :yin.k/stream\n                                    :yin.k/request)))\n            enrolled? (contains? (:enrolled @found) target)\n            carried? (some? (:op-id entry))]\n        (cond\n          (and enrolled? (not carried?))\n          (non-portable! :unprotected-pending {:dao.stream/identity target})\n\n          (and carried? (not enrolled?))\n          (unsatisfied! target)\n\n          carried?\n          (assoc pending :yin.k/op-id (:op-id entry))\n\n          :else pending)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Lift: one pending variant each, from the observed entry\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- call-out-cell\n  \"The emitter's call-out cursor cell -- the response route a retained\n   call held.  nil when the composition holds no call pair, which no\n   real retained request does.\"\n  [resources]\n  (let [cursor (get resources vm/call-out-cursor-key)\n        handle (get resources vm/call-out-stream-key)]\n    (when (and (map? cursor) (contains? cursor :stream-id) handle)\n      {:id vm/call-out-cursor-key\n       :stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key\n       :cursor (:cursor cursor)})))\n\n\n(defn- lift-pending!\n  \"The S7.4.3 pending of one observed entry, in `yin.vm.ucf.remote`'s\n   wire shapes, minted through THIS export's one cell and marker maps:\n   the cell a waiter names is the same cell a closure or the store\n   reaches, and the response route a retained call held is a cell like\n   any other, at its kept position.\"\n  [vm serve! found encode entry]\n  (case (observed-wire entry (:engine (:v2 @found)))\n    :next\n    {:yin.k/reason :next\n     :yin.k/cell (cell-for! vm serve! found\n                            (get-in entry [:cursor-ref :id]))}\n\n    :ffi\n    (cond-> {:yin.k/reason :ffi\n             :yin.k/call-id (entry-call-id (:engine (:v2 @found)) entry)\n             :yin.k/cell (cell-for! vm serve! found\n                                    (get-in entry [:cursor-ref :id]))}\n      (contains? entry :op) (assoc :yin.k/op (:op entry)))\n\n    :put\n    (do (when-not (contains? entry :datom)\n          (non-portable! :incomplete-write\n                         {:yin.k/pc (:pc entry)}))\n        {:yin.k/reason :put\n         :yin.k/stream (marker-for! vm serve! found (:stream-id entry))\n         :yin.k/value (encode (:datom entry))})\n\n    :ffi-request\n    (let [route (if (and (:response-cursor entry)\n                         (:response-stream entry)\n                         (:yin.k/recovery-cell-ids vm))\n                  {:id (:response-cursor entry)\n                   :stream-id (:response-stream entry)}\n                  (call-out-cell (:resources vm)))]\n      (if (nil? route)\n        (unsatisfied!)\n        (let [envelope (:datom entry)]\n          {:yin.k/reason :ffi-request\n           :yin.k/call-id (entry-call-id (:engine (:v2 @found)) entry)\n           :yin.k/request-envelope (encode envelope)\n           :yin.k/request-op (or (apply2/request-op envelope)\n                                 (:op entry)\n                                 (:op (:k entry)))\n           :yin.k/request-args (apply2/request-args envelope)\n           :yin.k/request (marker-for! vm serve! found\n                                       (:stream-id entry))\n           :yin.k/response (marker-for! vm serve! found\n                                        (:stream-id route))\n           :yin.k/response-cell (cell-for! vm serve! found\n                                           (:id route))})))\n\n    (:link-request :link-response)\n    (let [reason (:reason entry)\n          kept (:cursor entry)]\n      (cond-> {:yin.k/reason reason\n               :yin.k/link-id (:link-id entry)\n               :yin.k/name (:name entry)\n               :yin.k/request (marker-for! vm serve! found\n                                           (:request entry))\n               :yin.k/response (marker-for! vm serve! found\n                                            (:response entry))\n               :yin.k/cell (cell-at! vm serve! found\n                                     [(:response entry) kept]\n                                     (:response entry) kept)}\n        (= :link-request reason)\n        (assoc :yin.k/envelope (encode (:envelope entry)))))\n\n    :install\n    (do (when-not (contains? (:installs vm) (:name entry))\n          (non-portable! :incomplete-install {:yin.k/name (:name entry)}))\n        {:yin.k/reason :install\n         :yin.k/name (:name entry)})\n\n    (undecodable! {:yin.k/reason (:reason entry)\n                   :yin.k/path [:yin.k/wait (:pc entry)]})))\n\n\n(declare pc-profile? site-op site-reasons module-decls)\n\n\n(defn- lift-frame!\n  \"One wait entry lifted: its registers and its pending, the dynamic\n   reason checked against the static kinds at its pc -- the kinds gate\n   eligibility only, and a variant they do not admit is evidence the\n   frame is not exportable here, never a wire reason to invent.\"\n  [vm serve! found encode entry]\n  (let [engine (:engine (:v2 @found))\n        pc? (pc-profile? engine)\n        walker? (= :walker engine)\n        kinds (when-not (or pc? walker?)\n                (safepoint-kinds-at vm (:segment entry) (:pc entry)))\n        wire (observed-wire entry engine)]\n    (when (nil? wire)\n      (undecodable! {:yin.k/reason (:reason entry)\n                     :yin.k/path [:yin.k/wait (:pc entry)]}))\n    (when-not (cond\n                walker? true\n                pc? (contains? (get site-reasons (site-op engine entry)) wire)\n                :else (some #(contains? (get wire-of-kind %) wire) kinds))\n      (non-portable! :reason-mismatch\n                     {:yin.k/pc (:pc entry)\n                      :yin.k/reason wire\n                      :yin.safepoint/kinds (vec kinds)}))\n    {:yin.k/registers (if-some [v2 (:v2 @found)]\n                        (registers-v2 (:engine v2) found encode vm entry)\n                        (encode-registers found encode vm entry))\n     :yin.k/pending (protected! found entry\n                                (lift-pending! vm serve! found encode\n                                               entry))}))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The install children: a whole child travels, or nothing does\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(declare export-task validate-body validate-body-v1 validate-body-v2\n         v2-body? resume-task resume-task*)\n\n\n(defn- portable-response?\n  \"True when install `response` survives the body's own codec.\"\n  [jing-codec? response]\n  (if jing-codec?\n    (try (jing.cbor/encode response) true\n         (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ false))\n    (cbor/portable-value? response)))\n\n\n(defn- export-installs\n  \"Each live install child of `vm` as its own handoff body beside the\n   response that spawned it, preserving the child's phase and waits\n   (14.1.1's :install row).  A child that cannot export itself refuses\n   the parent's export -- a refusal is thrown, never embedded -- and a\n   response outside the canonical bytes domain refuses it too.  Under\n   version 1 the child is a part of its root's task: it carries the\n   root's version and enrolled set, no header, and its phase, a wire\n   phase (`:running` or `:parked`), and parent always travel.\"\n  [vm serve! opts]\n  (let [jing-codec? (::jing-codec opts)]\n    (into {}\n          (map (fn [[m {:keys [vm phase parent response]}]]\n                 (when-not (portable-response? jing-codec? response)\n                   (non-portable! :install-response {:yin.k/name m}))\n                 (when (and jing-codec? (not (contains? #{:running :parked} phase)))\n                   (non-portable! :incomplete-install\n                                  {:yin.k/name m :yin.k/phase phase}))\n                 (let [r (export-task vm serve!\n                                      (assoc opts\n                                             :path (conj (:path opts) m)\n                                             ::child true))]\n                   (when (not= :ok (:status r))\n                     (refuse! (:yin.k/status r) (dissoc r :status)))\n                   [m {:yin.k/phase phase\n                       :yin.k/parent parent\n                       :yin.k/response response\n                       :yin.k/child (:body r)}])))\n          (:installs vm))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Version 2 lift: one adapter per execution profile (UCF v2 amendment)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- engine-of\n  \"The version-2 engine of `vm`, from the kernel's own link format: the\n   profile is the kernel's, never inferred from an image's shape.\"","numLines":840,"startLine":1,"totalLines":3784}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SXhMG8DC58tVbjieH2qSHx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
