{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RTyrQES6dphLHR6MCiifye","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.safepoint-harness-test\n2\t  \"D16-prep: the safepoint conformance harness (UCF 7.4.1; 7.11.1's\n3\t   safepoint-reconstruction row and its acceptance blocker; linker-dht\n4\t   14.1.1 and 14.1.3's second row).\n5\t\n6\t   Every corpus segment is run to every liftable row of 7.4.1 -- explicit\n7\t   park, blocked read, blocked write, sent FFI, retained FFI, ordinary and\n8\t   tail effectful calls, halt -- on both fork body versions: version 0\n9\t   (the semantic profile, the only one it speaks) and version 2 (the four\n10\t   profiles).  The corpus wraps each row's parking expression in four\n11\t   segments: bare, as an operand, three ordinary activations deep, and\n12\t   inside a closure called with a captured environment.\n13\t\n14\t   Each case builds the same program twice.  The reference build is\n15\t   satisfied and run on its own machine; the handoff build is lifted to\n16\t   canonical bytes, lowered into a fresh machine over the toy channel,\n17\t   satisfied through the source's streams and run through the\n18\t   reflections.  Result and effect trace must agree; `lift(lower(frame))`\n19\t   must reproduce the lifted body; the frame's reason is the observed\n20\t   wait's.  An explicit park is checked through its parked record: no\n21\t   frame, the record by its own id, the controlled `:vm/resume`.  Halt is\n22\t   a result, not a frame.\n23\t\n24\t   Beside the matrix: one pc reached by two activations of different\n25\t   depth and captured environment, handed off at each; a nonempty ready\n26\t   queue; a kept FFI response cursor shared by two waiters; and a real\n27\t   held immediate (the D4 `:observe` entry), which refuses export.\"\n28\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n29\t            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n30\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n31\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n32\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n33\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n34\t            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n35\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n36\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n37\t            [yin.vm.ucf.handoff :as handoff]\n38\t            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as support]\n39\t            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]))\n40\t\n41\t\n42\t(def ^:private lanes\n43\t  \"Every [profile version] pair: version 0 speaks the semantic profile\n44\t   only; version 2 all four.\"\n45\t  (into [[:semantic 0]] (map (fn [e] [e 2])) s/engines))\n46\t\n47\t\n48\t(defn- lift\n49\t  \"The fork lift of `m` at `version` over `peer`'s served table.\"\n50\t  [m version t peer surfaces]\n51\t  (handoff/export-task m (s/server peer (:channel t) surfaces)\n52\t                       (when (= 2 version) {:version 2})))\n53\t\n54\t\n55\t(defn- drive-peers\n56\t  \"Run `m` through its reflections, stepping every peer's mirror between\n57\t   rounds, until it stops blocking.\"\n58\t  [m peers rounds]\n59\t  (loop [m (vm/run m), n rounds]\n60\t    (if (or (not (vm/blocked? m)) (zero? n))\n61\t      m\n62\t      (do (run! s/serve-mirror! peers)\n63\t          (recur (vm/run m) (dec n))))))\n64\t\n65\t\n66\t;; =============================================================================\n67\t;; The corpus: four segments around one parking expression\n68\t;; =============================================================================\n69\t\n70\t(defn- with-cat\n71\t  \"`ast` with `cat`, a closure conj-ing its two arguments, in scope.  The\n72\t   corpus combines through it, not through the `conj` primitive: the\n73\t   register profile cannot resume a wait whose live registers hold a\n74\t   host primitive (`:continuation-registers`, reported with D16-prep),\n75\t   and a closure keeps that defect out of every other row's evidence.\"\n76\t  [ast]\n77\t  (s/let1 'cat (s/lam ['p 'q] (s/app (s/v 'conj) (s/v 'p) (s/v 'q))) ast))\n78\t\n79\t\n80\t(defn- cat-of\n81\t  [p q]\n82\t  (s/app (s/v 'cat) p q))\n83\t\n84\t\n85\t(defn- nest\n86\t  \"`op` inside `d` ordinary (non-tail) closure activations.\"\n87\t  [d op]\n88\t  (if (zero? d)\n89\t    op\n90\t    (cat-of (s/lit [d]) (s/app (s/lam ['x] (nest (dec d) op)) (s/lit d)))))\n91\t\n92\t\n93\t(def ^:private corpus\n94\t  \"Each segment binds `cat` around its whole body, so a row's parking\n95\t   expression may combine through it too.\"\n96\t  (mapv\n97\t    (fn [[label seg]] [label (comp with-cat seg)])\n98\t    [[:bare identity]\n99\t     [:operand (fn [op] (cat-of (s/lit [:operand]) op))]\n100\t     [:depth-3 (fn [op] (nest 3 op))]\n101\t     [:captured\n102\t      (fn [op]\n103\t        (s/let1 'k (s/lit :captured)\n104\t                (s/let1 'f (s/lam ['y] (cat-of (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'k))\n105\t                                                       (s/v 'y))\n106\t                                               op))\n107\t                        (s/app (s/v 'f) (s/lit :arg)))))]]))\n108\t\n109\t\n110\t;; =============================================================================\n111\t;; The rows: one builder per 7.4.1 row\n112\t;; =============================================================================\n113\t;;\n114\t;; A builder answers the parked machine and how to satisfy its wait: the\n115\t;; steps run in order, each followed by a drive; `:finish` and the\n116\t;; receiver's own `:finish` record the effect trace into `:trace`.\n117\t\n118\t(defn- read-row\n119\t  \"A blocked read at a kept position: A consumed, B unread.\"\n120\t  [engine seg]\n121\t  (let [m0 (vm/run (s/load-ast\n122\t                     engine (s/new-machine engine)\n123\t                     (s/let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n124\t                             (s/let1 'c (s/cursor-of (s/v 's))\n125\t                                     (seg (s/let1 'a (s/next-of (s/v 'c))\n126\t                                                  (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'a))\n127\t                                                          (s/next-of (s/v 'c)))))))))\n128\t        src (s/stream-of m0)]\n129\t    (stream/append! src \"A\")\n130\t    {:machine (vm/run m0)\n131\t     :kind :blocked\n132\t     :reason :next\n133\t     :steps [#(stream/append! src \"B\")]\n134\t     :trace (atom [])}))\n135\t\n136\t\n137\t(defn- write-row\n138\t  \"A blocked write: the one-slot target is warm, the value retained.\"\n139\t  [engine seg]\n140\t  (let [trace (atom [])\n141\t        w (support/one-slot-stream \"w\")\n142\t        _ (stream/append! w :warmed)\n143\t        m0 (s/load-ast engine (s/new-machine engine)\n144\t                       (seg {:type :stream/put, :target (s/v 'w),\n145\t                             :val (s/lit \"v\")}))\n146\t        [ref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)\n147\t        take! #(swap! trace conj (:dao.stream/value (stream/next w 0)))]\n148\t    {:machine (vm/run (assoc m1 :store {'w ref}))\n149\t     :kind :blocked\n150\t     :reason :put\n151\t     :surfaces #{:reader :writer}\n152\t     :steps [take!]\n153\t     :finish take!\n154\t     :trace trace}))\n155\t\n156\t\n157\t(defn- own-call-pair\n158\t  \"The receiver's own FFI pair: a subsequent call uses it, so the trace\n159\t   records what it carried.\"\n160\t  [trace]\n161\t  (let [own-in (s/ring 8)\n162\t        own-out (s/ring 8)]\n163\t    {:opts {:call-in own-in\n164\t            :call-out own-out\n165\t            :call-out-cursor (vm/mint-oldest own-out :test)}\n166\t     :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain own-in))}))\n167\t\n168\t\n169\t(defn- sent-ffi-row\n170\t  \"A sent FFI call awaiting its correlated response.\"\n171\t  [engine seg]\n172\t  (let [trace (atom [])\n173\t        call-in (s/ring 8)\n174\t        call-out (s/ring 8)\n175\t        m (vm/run (s/load-ast engine (s/calling-machine engine call-in call-out)\n176\t                              (seg (s/call-node :op/echo \"hello\"))))\n177\t        id (ffi/response-call-id (first (:wait-set m)))]\n178\t    {:machine m\n179\t     :kind :blocked\n180\t     :reason :ffi\n181\t     :steps [#(stream/append! call-out (apply2/success-response id \"echo!\"))]\n182\t     :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain call-in))\n183\t     :receiver #(own-call-pair trace)\n184\t     :trace trace}))\n185\t\n186\t\n187\t(defn- retained-ffi-row\n188\t  \"An FFI request retained behind a full call-in; once the slot frees,\n189\t   the retry lands and the response correlates.\"\n190\t  [engine seg]\n191\t  (let [trace (atom [])\n192\t        call-in (support/one-slot-stream \"call-in\")\n193\t        call-out (s/ring 8)\n194\t        _ (stream/append! call-in :warmed)\n195\t        m (vm/run (s/load-ast engine (s/calling-machine engine call-in call-out)\n196\t                              (seg (s/call-node :op/echo \"hello\"))))\n197\t        id (ffi/request-call-id (first (:wait-set m)))]\n198\t    {:machine m\n199\t     :kind :blocked\n200\t     :reason :ffi-request\n201\t     :surfaces #{:reader :writer}\n202\t     :steps [#(stream/next call-in 0)\n203\t             (fn []\n204\t               (swap! trace conj (:dao.stream/value (stream/next call-in 0)))\n205\t               (stream/append! call-out (apply2/success-response id \"echo!\")))]\n206\t     :receiver #(own-call-pair trace)\n207\t     :trace trace}))\n208\t\n209\t\n210\t(defn- plain-module-response\n211\t  \"The `:ok` link response for `host.mod` exporting `f`, whose\n212\t   initialization blocks on nothing.\"\n213\t  [engine]\n214\t  {:status :ok\n215\t   :image {:value (s/module-image engine (s/def! 'f (s/lam [] (s/lit 42))))}\n216\t   :manifest {:yin.module/name 'host.mod\n217\t              :yin.module/exports #{'f}}\n218\t   :obligations []})\n219\t\n220\t\n221\t(defn- require-row\n222\t  \"An effectful call of `require` -- ordinary, or `tail?` in the tail\n223\t   position of a closure -- parked polling for its link response.\"\n224\t  [tail?]\n225\t  (fn [engine seg]\n226\t    (let [trace (atom [])\n227\t          request (s/ring 64)\n228\t          response (s/ring 64)\n229\t          call (cond-> (s/require-program 'host.mod) tail? (assoc :tail? true))\n230\t          op (if tail? (s/app (s/lam ['u] call) (s/lit 0)) call)\n231\t          m (vm/run (s/load-ast engine (s/linking-machine engine request response)\n232\t                                (seg op)))\n233\t          id (:link-id (first (:wait-set m)))]\n234\t      {:machine m\n235\t       :kind :blocked\n236\t       :reason :link-response\n237\t       :steps [#(stream/append! response\n238\t                                (assoc (plain-module-response engine)\n239\t                                       :yin.link/id id))]\n240\t       :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain request))\n241\t       :receiver (fn []\n242\t                   (let [rq (s/ring 64)]\n243\t                     {:opts {:link-request rq :link-response (s/ring 64)}\n244\t                      :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain rq))}))\n245\t       :trace trace})))\n246\t\n247\t\n248\t(def ^:private stream-modules\n249\t  (module/register-stream-module (module/default-registry)))\n250\t\n251\t\n252\t(defn- stream-call-row\n253\t  \"An effectful call of the stream module's `next!` -- ordinary, or\n254\t   `tail?` in the tail position of a closure -- parked on its read.\"\n255\t  [tail?]\n256\t  (fn [engine seg]\n257\t    (let [call (cond-> (s/app (s/v 'stream/next!) (s/v 'c)) tail? (assoc :tail? true))\n258\t          op (if tail?\n259\t               (s/app (s/lam ['u] call) (s/lit 0))\n260\t               (cat-of (s/lit [:ordinary]) call))\n261\t          m (vm/run (s/load-ast engine (s/new-machine engine {:modules stream-modules})\n262\t                                (s/let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n263\t                                        (s/let1 'c (s/cursor-of (s/v 's))\n264\t                                                (seg op)))))\n265\t          src (s/stream-of m)]\n266\t      {:machine m\n267\t       :kind :blocked\n268\t       :reason :next\n269\t       :steps [#(stream/append! src \"B\")]\n270\t       :receiver (constantly {:opts {:modules stream-modules}})\n271\t       :trace (atom [])})))\n272\t\n273\t\n274\t(defn- park-row\n275\t  \"An explicit park: resumed by its record's id, not by a wait.\"\n276\t  [engine seg]\n277\t  (let [m (vm/run (s/load-ast engine (s/new-machine engine) (seg {:type :vm/park})))\n278\t        pid (:id (vm/value m))]\n279\t    {:machine m\n280\t     :kind :parked\n281\t     :resume (fn [m']\n282\t               (s/run-beside engine m' {:type :vm/resume, :parked-id pid,\n283\t                                        :val (s/lit \"back\")}))\n284\t     :trace (atom [])}))\n285\t\n286\t\n287\t(defn- halt-row\n288\t  [engine seg]\n289\t  {:machine (vm/run (s/load-ast engine (s/new-machine engine) (seg (s/lit 42))))\n290\t   :kind :halted\n291\t   :trace (atom [])})\n292\t\n293\t\n294\t(def ^:private rows\n295\t  \"The liftable rows of 7.4.1, by name: every row runs on every lane.\"\n296\t  [[:explicit-park park-row]\n297\t   [:blocked-read read-row]\n298\t   [:blocked-write write-row]\n299\t   [:sent-ffi sent-ffi-row]\n300\t   [:retained-ffi retained-ffi-row]\n301\t   [:ordinary-require (require-row false)]\n302\t   [:tail-require (require-row true)]\n303\t   [:ordinary-stream-call (stream-call-row false)]\n304\t   [:tail-stream-call (stream-call-row true)]\n305\t   [:halt halt-row]])\n306\t\n307\t\n308\t;; =============================================================================\n309\t;; Open defects: production behavior the harness found, pinned as canaries\n310\t;; =============================================================================\n311\t\n312\t(def ^:private open-defects\n313\t  \"Production defects this harness found (D16-prep findings D1 to D4),\n314\t   by [profile row-or-check] and the checks each breaks.  A listed check\n315\t   asserts the defect is still there, so the fix fails its canary and the\n316\t   entry is removed with it; every unlisted check holds.\n317\t\n318\t   D1 :export -- the semantic lift censuses the stream module's host\n319\t   footprint as undeclared and refuses `:yin.k/unsatisfied`\n320\t   (`:incomplete`), so its effectful calls cannot lift there.\n321\t   D2 :relift -- a lowered retained FFI request relifts with the\n322\t   receiver's own call-out position as its response cell, not the\n323\t   carried one.\n324\t   D3 :result -- on stack and register, the retried request of a\n325\t   lowered retained FFI call then waits on the receiver's own call-out,\n326\t   so the emitter's correlated response never wakes it.\n327\t   D4 :source-acceptance -- a lowered blocked writer completes on the\n328\t   reflection's outbound acceptance while the source target is still\n329\t   full, and the retained value never reaches it (14.1.1).\n330\t   D0 :live-primitive -- the register profile refuses to resume any wait\n331\t   whose live registers hold a host primitive, with no handoff at all\n332\t   (`:continuation-registers`); the corpus combines through a closure\n333\t   for that reason.\"\n334\t  {[:register :live-primitive] #{:resume}\n335\t   [:semantic :ordinary-stream-call] #{:export}\n336\t   [:semantic :tail-stream-call] #{:export}\n337\t   [:semantic :retained-ffi] #{:relift}\n338\t   [:stack :retained-ffi] #{:relift :result}\n339\t   [:register :retained-ffi] #{:relift :result}\n340\t   [:semantic :writer] #{:source-acceptance}\n341\t   [:stack :writer] #{:source-acceptance}\n342\t   [:register :writer] #{:source-acceptance}\n343\t   [:walker :writer] #{:source-acceptance}})\n344\t\n345\t\n346\t(defn- check\n347\t  \"Assert `ok?` -- or, for an open defect of `engine` and `row`, that the\n348\t   defect still holds.\"\n349\t  [engine row k ok? msg]\n350\t  (if (contains? (get open-defects [engine row]) k)\n351\t    (is (not ok?) (str \"open defect \" k \" of \" (name engine) \" \" (name row)\n352\t                       \" no longer reproduces: remove it from open-defects\"))\n353\t    (is ok? msg)))\n354\t\n355\t\n356\t;; =============================================================================\n357\t;; The two runs\n358\t;; =============================================================================\n359\t\n360\t(defn- satisfy\n361\t  \"Run the row's steps over `m`, each followed by `drive`, or its\n362\t   controlled resume.\"\n363\t  [world m drive]\n364\t  (if-let [resume (:resume world)]\n365\t    (resume m)\n366\t    (reduce (fn [m step] (step) (drive m)) m (:steps world))))\n367\t\n368\t\n369\t(defn- reference\n370\t  [world]\n371\t  (let [done (satisfy world (:machine world) #(s/drive-local % 6))]\n372\t    (when-let [f (:finish world)] (f))\n373\t    {:halted (vm/halted? done), :value (vm/value done), :trace @(:trace world)}))\n374\t\n375\t\n376\t(defn- handed-off\n377\t  \"Lift the row's machine, lower it into a fresh receiver, relift that\n378\t   receiver at once, then satisfy the wait through the source's streams.\n379\t   The mirror is stepped once more after the run: a lowered writer's\n380\t   append reaches the source only through the mirror (see D4).\"\n381\t  [engine version world]\n382\t  (let [t (s/toy)\n383\t        peer (s/served-peer t)\n384\t        surfaces (or (:surfaces world) #{:reader})\n385\t        export (lift (:machine world) version t peer surfaces)\n386\t        receiver ((or (:receiver world) (constantly nil)))\n387\t        attach! (s/attacher t)\n388\t        r (when (= :ok (:status export))\n389\t            (handoff/resume-task\n390\t              (s/new-machine engine (merge {:attach-stream attach!}\n391\t                                           (:opts receiver)))\n392\t              (:bytes export) attach! {:address (:address export)}))\n393\t        recv (:vm r)\n394\t        t2 (s/toy)\n395\t        relift (when recv (lift recv version t2 (s/served-peer t2) surfaces))\n396\t        done (when recv (satisfy world recv #(drive-peers % [peer] 6)))\n397\t        _ (s/serve-mirror! peer)]\n398\t    (when-let [f (:finish world)] (f))\n399\t    (when-let [f (:finish receiver)] (f))\n400\t    {:export export, :lower r, :recv recv, :relift relift,\n401\t     :halted (some-> done vm/halted?), :value (some-> done vm/value),\n402\t     :trace @(:trace world)}))\n403\t\n404\t\n405\t(defn- frame-pending\n406\t  [export]\n407\t  (get-in export [:body :yin.k/frames 0 :yin.k/pending]))\n408\t\n409\t\n410\t(defn- kind-checks\n411\t  \"The row kind's own observables: a blocked frame's reason is the\n412\t   observed wait's; an explicit park is its parked record; a halt is a\n413\t   result.\"\n414\t  [world expected export recv]\n415\t  (let [body (:body export)]\n416\t    (case (:kind world)\n417\t      :blocked\n418\t      (is (= (:reason world) (:yin.k/reason (frame-pending export)))\n419\t          \"the frame's reason is the observed wait's\")\n420\t      :parked\n421\t      (let [pid (:id (vm/value (:machine world)))]\n422\t        (is (empty? (:yin.k/frames body))\n423\t            \"an explicit park mints no pending wait\")\n424\t        (is (contains? (:yin.k/parked body) pid))\n425\t        (is (= pid (:id (vm/value recv)))\n426\t            \"the active park is the source's record, by its own id\")\n427\t        (is (= (vm/value recv) (get (:parked recv) pid))))\n428\t      :halted\n429\t      (do (is (not (contains? body :yin.k/frames)))\n430\t          (is (= (:value expected) (:yin.k/result body))\n431\t              \"halt carries the result\")\n432\t          (is (vm/halted? recv))\n433\t          (is (empty? (:wait-set recv)))))))\n434\t\n435\t\n436\t(deftest ^:slow every-corpus-segment-to-every-row-matches-the-reference\n437\t  (slow/guard\n438\t    \"every-corpus-segment-to-every-row-matches-the-reference\"\n439\t    (fn []\n440\t      (doseq [[engine version] lanes\n441\t              [row build] rows\n442\t              [seg wrap] corpus]\n443\t        (testing (str (name engine) \" v\" version \" \" (name row) \" \" (name seg))\n444\t          (let [expected (reference (build engine wrap))\n445\t                world (build engine wrap)\n446\t                {:keys [export lower recv relift] :as got}\n447\t                (handed-off engine version world)\n448\t                body (:body export)]\n449\t            (is (:halted expected) \"the reference run completes\")\n450\t            (check engine row :export (= :ok (:status export)) (pr-str export))\n451\t            (when (= :ok (:status export))\n452\t              (is (= (:kind world) (:kind export)))\n453\t              (is (= version (:yin.k/version body)))\n454\t              (kind-checks world expected export recv)\n455\t              (is (= :ok (:status lower)) (pr-str lower))\n456\t              (is (= :ok (:status relift)) (pr-str relift))\n457\t              (check engine row :relift\n458\t                     (= (s/stream-blind body) (s/stream-blind (:body relift)))\n459\t                     \"lift(lower(frame)) reproduces the canonical body\")\n460\t              (check engine row :result\n461\t                     (= (select-keys expected [:halted :value :trace])\n462\t                        (select-keys got [:halted :value :trace]))\n463\t                     \"result and effect trace equal the reference run\"))))))))\n464\t\n465\t\n466\t(deftest a-wait-over-a-live-host-primitive-resumes-on-every-profile\n467\t  ;; no handoff: the reference machine alone, `conj` pending as an operand\n468\t  (doseq [engine s/engines]\n469\t    (testing (name engine)\n470\t      (let [m0 (vm/run (s/load-ast\n471\t                         engine (s/new-machine engine)\n472\t                         (s/let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n473\t                                 (s/let1 'c (s/cursor-of (s/v 's))\n474\t                                         (s/app (s/v 'conj) (s/lit [])\n475\t                                                (s/next-of (s/v 'c)))))))\n476\t            _ (stream/append! (s/stream-of m0) \"A\")\n477\t            done (try (vm/run m0)\n478\t                      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) _\n479\t                        nil))]\n480\t        (check engine :live-primitive :resume\n481\t               (and (some? done) (= [\"A\"] (vm/value done)))\n482\t               \"the read wakes and the primitive applies\")))))\n483\t\n484\t\n485\t;; =============================================================================\n486\t;; Ordinary and tail effectful calls are what they claim\n487\t;; =============================================================================\n488\t\n489\t(deftest the-tail-rows-park-in-a-tail-call\n490\t  (doseq [[row build] [[:ordinary-require (require-row false)]\n491\t                       [:tail-require (require-row true)]\n492\t                       [:ordinary-stream-call (stream-call-row false)]\n493\t                       [:tail-stream-call (stream-call-row true)]]\n494\t          [seg wrap] corpus]\n495\t    (testing (str (name row) \" \" (name seg))\n496\t      (let [m (:machine (build :semantic wrap))\n497\t            entry (first (:wait-set m))\n498\t            site (get-in m [:code (:segment entry) :code (dec (:pc entry))])]\n499\t        (is (= (if (#{:tail-require :tail-stream-call} row)\n500\t                 (:tailcall vm/opcode-table)\n501\t                 (:call vm/opcode-table))\n502\t               (first site))\n503\t            (str \"the parking instruction \" (pr-str site)))))))\n504\t\n505\t\n506\t;; =============================================================================\n507\t;; One pc, two activations: distinct depth and captured environment\n508\t;; =============================================================================\n509\t\n510\t(defn- two-activations\n511\t  \"One reading closure body, reached twice: through `g1` (captured\n512\t   `:one`) as an operand, then through `g2` (captured `:two`) two\n513\t   ordinary activations deeper.  Answers [parked source].\"\n514\t  [engine]\n515\t  (let [reader (s/lam ['k]\n516\t                      (s/lam ['y]\n517\t                             (cat-of (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'k)) (s/v 'y))\n518\t                                     (s/next-of (s/v 'c)))))\n519\t        body (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/app (s/v 'g1) (s/lit 1)))\n520\t                     (nest 2 (s/app (s/v 'g2) (s/lit 2))))\n521\t        m (vm/run\n522\t            (s/load-ast\n523\t              engine (s/new-machine engine)\n524\t              (with-cat\n525\t                (s/let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n526\t                        (s/let1 'c (s/cursor-of (s/v 's))\n527\t                                (s/let1 'mk reader\n528\t                                        (s/let1 'g1 (s/app (s/v 'mk) (s/lit :one))\n529\t                                                (s/let1 'g2 (s/app (s/v 'mk) (s/lit :two))\n530\t                                                        body))))))))]\n531\t    [m (s/stream-of m)]))\n532\t\n533\t\n534\t(defn- registers\n535\t  [export]\n536\t  (get-in export [:body :yin.k/frames 0 :yin.k/registers]))\n537\t\n538\t\n539\t(deftest ^:slow one-pc-reached-at-two-depths-hands-off-at-each\n540\t  (slow/guard\n541\t    \"one-pc-reached-at-two-depths-hands-off-at-each\"\n542\t    (fn []\n543\t      (doseq [[engine version] lanes]\n544\t        (testing (str (name engine) \" v\" version)\n545\t          (let [[ref-m ref-src] (two-activations engine)\n546\t                _ (stream/append! ref-src \"B\")\n547\t                ref-hop (s/drive-local ref-m 6)\n548\t                _ (stream/append! ref-src \"C\")\n549\t                expected (vm/value (s/drive-local ref-hop 6))\n550\t                [m src] (two-activations engine)\n551\t                t1 (s/toy)\n552\t                p1 (s/served-peer t1)\n553\t                e1 (lift m version t1 p1 #{:reader})\n554\t                r1 (:vm (handoff/resume-task\n555\t                          (s/new-machine engine {:attach-stream (s/attacher t1)})\n556\t                          (:bytes e1) (s/attacher t1) {:address (:address e1)}))\n557\t                _ (stream/append! src \"B\")\n558\t                hop (drive-peers r1 [p1] 6)\n559\t                t2 (s/toy)\n560\t                p2 (s/served-peer t2)\n561\t                e2 (lift hop version t2 p2 #{:reader})\n562\t                r2 (:vm (handoff/resume-task\n563\t                          (s/new-machine engine {:attach-stream (s/attacher t2)})\n564\t                          (:bytes e2) (s/attacher t2) {:address (:address e2)}))\n565\t                _ (stream/append! src \"C\")\n566\t                done (drive-peers r2 [p2 p1] 8)\n567\t                regs1 (registers e1)\n568\t                regs2 (registers e2)]\n569\t            (is (= :ok (:status e1)) (pr-str e1))\n570\t            (is (= :ok (:status e2)) (pr-str e2))\n571\t            (is (= [:next :next] (mapv (comp :yin.k/reason frame-pending) [e1 e2])))\n572\t            ;; the walker's frame is its environment and continuation alone:\n573\t            ;; it has no pc to compare\n574\t            (when-not (= :walker engine)\n575\t              (is (some? (:yin.k/pc regs1)))\n576\t              (is (= (select-keys regs1 [:yin.k/pc :yin.k/segment :yin.k/image])\n577\t                     (select-keys regs2 [:yin.k/pc :yin.k/segment :yin.k/image]))\n578\t                  \"both hand-offs park at one pc of one segment\"))\n579\t            (is (not= regs1 regs2)\n580\t                \"with a different activation: depth and captured environment\")\n581\t            (is (= [[:one 1 \"B\"] [2 [1 [:two 2 \"C\"]]]] expected))\n582\t            (is (vm/halted? done))\n583\t            (is (= expected (vm/value done))\n584\t                \"two hand-offs answer what the source's own run did\")))))))\n585\t\n586\t\n587\t;; =============================================================================\n588\t;; Queued work, a shared response cursor, a held immediate, the writer\n589\t;; =============================================================================\n590\t\n591\t(defn- counting-server\n592\t  [t peer surfaces]\n593\t  (let [n (atom 0)\n594\t        serve! (s/server peer (:channel t) surfaces)]\n595\t    [(fn [h] (swap! n inc) (serve! h)) n]))\n596\t\n597\t\n598\t(deftest a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-not-quiescent\n599\t  (doseq [[engine version] lanes]\n600\t    (testing (str (name engine) \" v\" version)\n601\t      (let [[parked src] (s/parked-reader engine)\n602\t            _ (stream/append! src \"B\")\n603\t            woken (engine/check-wait-set parked)\n604\t            t (s/toy)\n605\t            [serve! n] (counting-server t (s/served-peer t) #{:reader})\n606\t            r (handoff/export-task woken serve! (when (= 2 version) {:version 2}))]\n607\t        (is (seq (:ready-queue woken)) \"the sweep queued the woken reader\")\n608\t        (is (= :yin.k/not-quiescent (:yin.k/status r)) (pr-str r))\n609\t        (is (not (contains? r :bytes)) \"nothing is published\")\n610\t        (is (zero? @n) \"no stream was served\")))))\n611\t\n612\t\n613\t(defn- two-callers\n614\t  \"A sent caller whose response cell is shared by a second outstanding\n615\t   call: the real waiter, and a second waiter built from it under its own\n616\t   call id -- the construction of the stage-1 alias row.  Answers\n617\t   [machine call-out].\"\n618\t  [engine]\n619\t  (let [[parked _ call-out] (s/parked-sent-caller engine)\n620\t        e1 (first (:wait-set parked))\n621\t        ;; the walker keeps the call id in its continuation as well\n622\t        e2 (cond-> (assoc e1 :call-id :parked-9)\n623\t             (contains? (:k e1) :call-id) (assoc-in [:k :call-id] :parked-9))]\n624\t    [(assoc parked :wait-set [e1 e2]) call-out]))\n625\t\n626\t\n627\t(defn- answer-both!\n628\t  \"The second call's response first, then the first's.\"\n629\t  [call-out]\n630\t  (stream/append! call-out (apply2/success-response :parked-9 \"second\"))\n631\t  (stream/append! call-out (apply2/success-response :parked-0 \"first\")))\n632\t\n633\t\n634\t(defn- sweep\n635\t  [m peers]\n636\t  (loop [m (engine/check-wait-set m) n 12]\n637\t    (if (or (zero? n) (empty? (:wait-set m)))\n638\t      m\n639\t      (do (run! s/serve-mirror! peers)\n640\t          (recur (engine/check-wait-set m) (dec n))))))\n641\t\n642\t\n643\t(deftest a-response-cursor-shared-by-two-waiters-crosses-as-one-cell\n644\t  (doseq [[engine version] lanes]\n645\t    (testing (str (name engine) \" v\" version)\n646\t      (let [[ref-m ref-out] (two-callers engine)\n647\t            _ (answer-both! ref-out)\n648\t            expected (mapv :value (:ready-queue (sweep ref-m [])))\n649\t            [m call-out] (two-callers engine)\n650\t            t (s/toy)\n651\t            peer (s/served-peer t)\n652\t            export (lift m version t peer #{:reader})\n653\t            pendings (mapv :yin.k/pending (get-in export [:body :yin.k/frames]))\n654\t            own-out (s/ring 8)\n655\t            recv (:vm (handoff/resume-task\n656\t                        (s/new-machine engine {:attach-stream (s/attacher t)\n657\t                                               :call-in (s/ring 8)\n658\t                                               :call-out own-out\n659\t                                               :call-out-cursor\n660\t                                               (vm/mint-oldest own-out :test)})\n661\t                        (:bytes export) (s/attacher t)\n662\t                        {:address (:address export)}))\n663\t            [w1 w2] (:wait-set recv)\n664\t            _ (answer-both! call-out)\n665\t            swept (sweep recv [peer])]\n666\t        (is (= :ok (:status export)) (pr-str export))\n667\t        (is (= [:ffi :ffi] (mapv :yin.k/reason pendings)))\n668\t        (is (= [:parked-0 :parked-9] (mapv :yin.k/call-id pendings)))\n669\t        (is (= 1 (count (get-in export [:body :yin.k/cells])))\n670\t            \"the two waiters name one cell\")\n671\t        (is (= (:cursor-ref w1) (:cursor-ref w2))\n672\t            \"the lower gives both waiters one fresh cursor entry\")\n673\t        (is (= [(apply2/success-response :parked-9 \"second\")\n674\t                (apply2/success-response :parked-0 \"first\")]\n675\t               expected)\n676\t            \"the reference: each waiter woke on its own correlated response\")\n677\t        (is (empty? (:wait-set swept)))\n678\t        (is (= expected (mapv :value (:ready-queue swept)))\n679\t            \"the receiver wakes the same waiters with the same responses\")))))\n680\t\n681\t\n682\t(deftest a-held-immediate-refuses-export\n683\t  (doseq [[engine version] lanes]\n684\t    (testing (str (name engine) \" v\" version)\n685\t      (let [m0 (s/load-ast engine (s/new-machine engine {:modules stream-modules})\n686\t                           (s/app (s/v 'stream/poll!) (s/v 'c)))\n687\t            [sref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 (s/ring 8))\n688\t            [cref m2] (engine/handle-cursor m1 {:stream sref} :k1)\n689\t            held (vm/run (assoc m2 :store {'c cref} :yin.k/gate :running))\n690\t            t (s/toy)\n691\t            [serve! n] (counting-server t (s/served-peer t) #{:reader})\n692\t            r (handoff/export-task held serve! (when (= 2 version) {:version 2}))]\n693\t        (is (= [:observe] (mapv :reason (:wait-set held)))\n694\t            \"the gated poll is held as the D4 :observe entry\")\n695\t        (is (= :yin.k/non-portable (:yin.k/status r)) (pr-str r))\n696\t        (is (= :reason-mismatch (:yin.k/kind r)))\n697\t        (is (= :observe (:yin.k/hold r)))\n698\t        (is (not (contains? r :bytes)))\n699\t        (is (zero? @n) \"refused before any stream was served\")))))\n700\t\n701\t\n702\t(deftest a-lowered-writer-completes-only-on-source-acceptance\n703\t  (doseq [[engine version] lanes]\n704\t    (testing (str (name engine) \" v\" version)\n705\t      (let [[parked w] (s/parked-writer engine)\n706\t            t (s/toy)\n707\t            peer (s/served-peer t)\n708\t            export (lift parked version t peer #{:reader :writer})\n709\t            recv (:vm (handoff/resume-task\n710\t                        (s/new-machine engine {:attach-stream (s/attacher t)})\n711\t                        (:bytes export) (s/attacher t)\n712\t                        {:address (:address export)}))\n713\t            ;; the source target stays full through the first drive\n714\t            done (drive-peers recv [peer] 6)\n715\t            _ (s/serve-mirror! peer)\n716\t            held (stream/next w 0)\n717\t            later (drive-peers done [peer] 6)\n718\t            _ (s/serve-mirror! peer)\n719\t            landed (stream/next w 0)]\n720\t        (is (= :ok (:status export)) (pr-str export))\n721\t        (is (= :warmed (:dao.stream/value held)))\n722\t        (check engine :writer :source-acceptance (vm/blocked? done)\n723\t               \"the retry stays parked while the source refuses it\")\n724\t        (check engine :writer :source-acceptance\n725\t               (and (vm/halted? later) (= \"v\" (:dao.stream/value landed)))\n726\t               \"once the source accepts, the retained value lands\")))))\n727\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee657710-cc1c-4c43-882b-5874c9a79051","uuid":"c36c56a9-58bb-468d-b074-1f4647c5f129","timestamp":"2026-10-12T15:53:25.890Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6b/test/yin/vm/ucf/safepoint_harness_test.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.safepoint-harness-test\n  \"D16-prep: the safepoint conformance harness (UCF 7.4.1; 7.11.1's\n   safepoint-reconstruction row and its acceptance blocker; linker-dht\n   14.1.1 and 14.1.3's second row).\n\n   Every corpus segment is run to every liftable row of 7.4.1 -- explicit\n   park, blocked read, blocked write, sent FFI, retained FFI, ordinary and\n   tail effectful calls, halt -- on both fork body versions: version 0\n   (the semantic profile, the only one it speaks) and version 2 (the four\n   profiles).  The corpus wraps each row's parking expression in four\n   segments: bare, as an operand, three ordinary activations deep, and\n   inside a closure called with a captured environment.\n\n   Each case builds the same program twice.  The reference build is\n   satisfied and run on its own machine; the handoff build is lifted to\n   canonical bytes, lowered into a fresh machine over the toy channel,\n   satisfied through the source's streams and run through the\n   reflections.  Result and effect trace must agree; `lift(lower(frame))`\n   must reproduce the lifted body; the frame's reason is the observed\n   wait's.  An explicit park is checked through its parked record: no\n   frame, the record by its own id, the controlled `:vm/resume`.  Halt is\n   a result, not a frame.\n\n   Beside the matrix: one pc reached by two activations of different\n   depth and captured environment, handed off at each; a nonempty ready\n   queue; a kept FFI response cursor shared by two waiters; and a real\n   held immediate (the D4 `:observe` entry), which refuses export.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.handoff :as handoff]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as support]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]))\n\n\n(def ^:private lanes\n  \"Every [profile version] pair: version 0 speaks the semantic profile\n   only; version 2 all four.\"\n  (into [[:semantic 0]] (map (fn [e] [e 2])) s/engines))\n\n\n(defn- lift\n  \"The fork lift of `m` at `version` over `peer`'s served table.\"\n  [m version t peer surfaces]\n  (handoff/export-task m (s/server peer (:channel t) surfaces)\n                       (when (= 2 version) {:version 2})))\n\n\n(defn- drive-peers\n  \"Run `m` through its reflections, stepping every peer's mirror between\n   rounds, until it stops blocking.\"\n  [m peers rounds]\n  (loop [m (vm/run m), n rounds]\n    (if (or (not (vm/blocked? m)) (zero? n))\n      m\n      (do (run! s/serve-mirror! peers)\n          (recur (vm/run m) (dec n))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The corpus: four segments around one parking expression\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- with-cat\n  \"`ast` with `cat`, a closure conj-ing its two arguments, in scope.  The\n   corpus combines through it, not through the `conj` primitive: the\n   register profile cannot resume a wait whose live registers hold a\n   host primitive (`:continuation-registers`, reported with D16-prep),\n   and a closure keeps that defect out of every other row's evidence.\"\n  [ast]\n  (s/let1 'cat (s/lam ['p 'q] (s/app (s/v 'conj) (s/v 'p) (s/v 'q))) ast))\n\n\n(defn- cat-of\n  [p q]\n  (s/app (s/v 'cat) p q))\n\n\n(defn- nest\n  \"`op` inside `d` ordinary (non-tail) closure activations.\"\n  [d op]\n  (if (zero? d)\n    op\n    (cat-of (s/lit [d]) (s/app (s/lam ['x] (nest (dec d) op)) (s/lit d)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private corpus\n  \"Each segment binds `cat` around its whole body, so a row's parking\n   expression may combine through it too.\"\n  (mapv\n    (fn [[label seg]] [label (comp with-cat seg)])\n    [[:bare identity]\n     [:operand (fn [op] (cat-of (s/lit [:operand]) op))]\n     [:depth-3 (fn [op] (nest 3 op))]\n     [:captured\n      (fn [op]\n        (s/let1 'k (s/lit :captured)\n                (s/let1 'f (s/lam ['y] (cat-of (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'k))\n                                                       (s/v 'y))\n                                               op))\n                        (s/app (s/v 'f) (s/lit :arg)))))]]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The rows: one builder per 7.4.1 row\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; A builder answers the parked machine and how to satisfy its wait: the\n;; steps run in order, each followed by a drive; `:finish` and the\n;; receiver's own `:finish` record the effect trace into `:trace`.\n\n(defn- read-row\n  \"A blocked read at a kept position: A consumed, B unread.\"\n  [engine seg]\n  (let [m0 (vm/run (s/load-ast\n                     engine (s/new-machine engine)\n                     (s/let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n                             (s/let1 'c (s/cursor-of (s/v 's))\n                                     (seg (s/let1 'a (s/next-of (s/v 'c))\n                                                  (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'a))\n                                                          (s/next-of (s/v 'c)))))))))\n        src (s/stream-of m0)]\n    (stream/append! src \"A\")\n    {:machine (vm/run m0)\n     :kind :blocked\n     :reason :next\n     :steps [#(stream/append! src \"B\")]\n     :trace (atom [])}))\n\n\n(defn- write-row\n  \"A blocked write: the one-slot target is warm, the value retained.\"\n  [engine seg]\n  (let [trace (atom [])\n        w (support/one-slot-stream \"w\")\n        _ (stream/append! w :warmed)\n        m0 (s/load-ast engine (s/new-machine engine)\n                       (seg {:type :stream/put, :target (s/v 'w),\n                             :val (s/lit \"v\")}))\n        [ref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)\n        take! #(swap! trace conj (:dao.stream/value (stream/next w 0)))]\n    {:machine (vm/run (assoc m1 :store {'w ref}))\n     :kind :blocked\n     :reason :put\n     :surfaces #{:reader :writer}\n     :steps [take!]\n     :finish take!\n     :trace trace}))\n\n\n(defn- own-call-pair\n  \"The receiver's own FFI pair: a subsequent call uses it, so the trace\n   records what it carried.\"\n  [trace]\n  (let [own-in (s/ring 8)\n        own-out (s/ring 8)]\n    {:opts {:call-in own-in\n            :call-out own-out\n            :call-out-cursor (vm/mint-oldest own-out :test)}\n     :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain own-in))}))\n\n\n(defn- sent-ffi-row\n  \"A sent FFI call awaiting its correlated response.\"\n  [engine seg]\n  (let [trace (atom [])\n        call-in (s/ring 8)\n        call-out (s/ring 8)\n        m (vm/run (s/load-ast engine (s/calling-machine engine call-in call-out)\n                              (seg (s/call-node :op/echo \"hello\"))))\n        id (ffi/response-call-id (first (:wait-set m)))]\n    {:machine m\n     :kind :blocked\n     :reason :ffi\n     :steps [#(stream/append! call-out (apply2/success-response id \"echo!\"))]\n     :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain call-in))\n     :receiver #(own-call-pair trace)\n     :trace trace}))\n\n\n(defn- retained-ffi-row\n  \"An FFI request retained behind a full call-in; once the slot frees,\n   the retry lands and the response correlates.\"\n  [engine seg]\n  (let [trace (atom [])\n        call-in (support/one-slot-stream \"call-in\")\n        call-out (s/ring 8)\n        _ (stream/append! call-in :warmed)\n        m (vm/run (s/load-ast engine (s/calling-machine engine call-in call-out)\n                              (seg (s/call-node :op/echo \"hello\"))))\n        id (ffi/request-call-id (first (:wait-set m)))]\n    {:machine m\n     :kind :blocked\n     :reason :ffi-request\n     :surfaces #{:reader :writer}\n     :steps [#(stream/next call-in 0)\n             (fn []\n               (swap! trace conj (:dao.stream/value (stream/next call-in 0)))\n               (stream/append! call-out (apply2/success-response id \"echo!\")))]\n     :receiver #(own-call-pair trace)\n     :trace trace}))\n\n\n(defn- plain-module-response\n  \"The `:ok` link response for `host.mod` exporting `f`, whose\n   initialization blocks on nothing.\"\n  [engine]\n  {:status :ok\n   :image {:value (s/module-image engine (s/def! 'f (s/lam [] (s/lit 42))))}\n   :manifest {:yin.module/name 'host.mod\n              :yin.module/exports #{'f}}\n   :obligations []})\n\n\n(defn- require-row\n  \"An effectful call of `require` -- ordinary, or `tail?` in the tail\n   position of a closure -- parked polling for its link response.\"\n  [tail?]\n  (fn [engine seg]\n    (let [trace (atom [])\n          request (s/ring 64)\n          response (s/ring 64)\n          call (cond-> (s/require-program 'host.mod) tail? (assoc :tail? true))\n          op (if tail? (s/app (s/lam ['u] call) (s/lit 0)) call)\n          m (vm/run (s/load-ast engine (s/linking-machine engine request response)\n                                (seg op)))\n          id (:link-id (first (:wait-set m)))]\n      {:machine m\n       :kind :blocked\n       :reason :link-response\n       :steps [#(stream/append! response\n                                (assoc (plain-module-response engine)\n                                       :yin.link/id id))]\n       :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain request))\n       :receiver (fn []\n                   (let [rq (s/ring 64)]\n                     {:opts {:link-request rq :link-response (s/ring 64)}\n                      :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain rq))}))\n       :trace trace})))\n\n\n(def ^:private stream-modules\n  (module/register-stream-module (module/default-registry)))\n\n\n(defn- stream-call-row\n  \"An effectful call of the stream module's `next!` -- ordinary, or\n   `tail?` in the tail position of a closure -- parked on its read.\"\n  [tail?]\n  (fn [engine seg]\n    (let [call (cond-> (s/app (s/v 'stream/next!) (s/v 'c)) tail? (assoc :tail? true))\n          op (if tail?\n               (s/app (s/lam ['u] call) (s/lit 0))\n               (cat-of (s/lit [:ordinary]) call))\n          m (vm/run (s/load-ast engine (s/new-machine engine {:modules stream-modules})\n                                (s/let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n                                        (s/let1 'c (s/cursor-of (s/v 's))\n                                                (seg op)))))\n          src (s/stream-of m)]\n      {:machine m\n       :kind :blocked\n       :reason :next\n       :steps [#(stream/append! src \"B\")]\n       :receiver (constantly {:opts {:modules stream-modules}})\n       :trace (atom [])})))\n\n\n(defn- park-row\n  \"An explicit park: resumed by its record's id, not by a wait.\"\n  [engine seg]\n  (let [m (vm/run (s/load-ast engine (s/new-machine engine) (seg {:type :vm/park})))\n        pid (:id (vm/value m))]\n    {:machine m\n     :kind :parked\n     :resume (fn [m']\n               (s/run-beside engine m' {:type :vm/resume, :parked-id pid,\n                                        :val (s/lit \"back\")}))\n     :trace (atom [])}))\n\n\n(defn- halt-row\n  [engine seg]\n  {:machine (vm/run (s/load-ast engine (s/new-machine engine) (seg (s/lit 42))))\n   :kind :halted\n   :trace (atom [])})\n\n\n(def ^:private rows\n  \"The liftable rows of 7.4.1, by name: every row runs on every lane.\"\n  [[:explicit-park park-row]\n   [:blocked-read read-row]\n   [:blocked-write write-row]\n   [:sent-ffi sent-ffi-row]\n   [:retained-ffi retained-ffi-row]\n   [:ordinary-require (require-row false)]\n   [:tail-require (require-row true)]\n   [:ordinary-stream-call (stream-call-row false)]\n   [:tail-stream-call (stream-call-row true)]\n   [:halt halt-row]])\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Open defects: production behavior the harness found, pinned as canaries\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private open-defects\n  \"Production defects this harness found (D16-prep findings D1 to D4),\n   by [profile row-or-check] and the checks each breaks.  A listed check\n   asserts the defect is still there, so the fix fails its canary and the\n   entry is removed with it; every unlisted check holds.\n\n   D1 :export -- the semantic lift censuses the stream module's host\n   footprint as undeclared and refuses `:yin.k/unsatisfied`\n   (`:incomplete`), so its effectful calls cannot lift there.\n   D2 :relift -- a lowered retained FFI request relifts with the\n   receiver's own call-out position as its response cell, not the\n   carried one.\n   D3 :result -- on stack and register, the retried request of a\n   lowered retained FFI call then waits on the receiver's own call-out,\n   so the emitter's correlated response never wakes it.\n   D4 :source-acceptance -- a lowered blocked writer completes on the\n   reflection's outbound acceptance while the source target is still\n   full, and the retained value never reaches it (14.1.1).\n   D0 :live-primitive -- the register profile refuses to resume any wait\n   whose live registers hold a host primitive, with no handoff at all\n   (`:continuation-registers`); the corpus combines through a closure\n   for that reason.\"\n  {[:register :live-primitive] #{:resume}\n   [:semantic :ordinary-stream-call] #{:export}\n   [:semantic :tail-stream-call] #{:export}\n   [:semantic :retained-ffi] #{:relift}\n   [:stack :retained-ffi] #{:relift :result}\n   [:register :retained-ffi] #{:relift :result}\n   [:semantic :writer] #{:source-acceptance}\n   [:stack :writer] #{:source-acceptance}\n   [:register :writer] #{:source-acceptance}\n   [:walker :writer] #{:source-acceptance}})\n\n\n(defn- check\n  \"Assert `ok?` -- or, for an open defect of `engine` and `row`, that the\n   defect still holds.\"\n  [engine row k ok? msg]\n  (if (contains? (get open-defects [engine row]) k)\n    (is (not ok?) (str \"open defect \" k \" of \" (name engine) \" \" (name row)\n                       \" no longer reproduces: remove it from open-defects\"))\n    (is ok? msg)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The two runs\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- satisfy\n  \"Run the row's steps over `m`, each followed by `drive`, or its\n   controlled resume.\"\n  [world m drive]\n  (if-let [resume (:resume world)]\n    (resume m)\n    (reduce (fn [m step] (step) (drive m)) m (:steps world))))\n\n\n(defn- reference\n  [world]\n  (let [done (satisfy world (:machine world) #(s/drive-local % 6))]\n    (when-let [f (:finish world)] (f))\n    {:halted (vm/halted? done), :value (vm/value done), :trace @(:trace world)}))\n\n\n(defn- handed-off\n  \"Lift the row's machine, lower it into a fresh receiver, relift that\n   receiver at once, then satisfy the wait through the source's streams.\n   The mirror is stepped once more after the run: a lowered writer's\n   append reaches the source only through the mirror (see D4).\"\n  [engine version world]\n  (let [t (s/toy)\n        peer (s/served-peer t)\n        surfaces (or (:surfaces world) #{:reader})\n        export (lift (:machine world) version t peer surfaces)\n        receiver ((or (:receiver world) (constantly nil)))\n        attach! (s/attacher t)\n        r (when (= :ok (:status export))\n            (handoff/resume-task\n              (s/new-machine engine (merge {:attach-stream attach!}\n                                           (:opts receiver)))\n              (:bytes export) attach! {:address (:address export)}))\n        recv (:vm r)\n        t2 (s/toy)\n        relift (when recv (lift recv version t2 (s/served-peer t2) surfaces))\n        done (when recv (satisfy world recv #(drive-peers % [peer] 6)))\n        _ (s/serve-mirror! peer)]\n    (when-let [f (:finish world)] (f))\n    (when-let [f (:finish receiver)] (f))\n    {:export export, :lower r, :recv recv, :relift relift,\n     :halted (some-> done vm/halted?), :value (some-> done vm/value),\n     :trace @(:trace world)}))\n\n\n(defn- frame-pending\n  [export]\n  (get-in export [:body :yin.k/frames 0 :yin.k/pending]))\n\n\n(defn- kind-checks\n  \"The row kind's own observables: a blocked frame's reason is the\n   observed wait's; an explicit park is its parked record; a halt is a\n   result.\"\n  [world expected export recv]\n  (let [body (:body export)]\n    (case (:kind world)\n      :blocked\n      (is (= (:reason world) (:yin.k/reason (frame-pending export)))\n          \"the frame's reason is the observed wait's\")\n      :parked\n      (let [pid (:id (vm/value (:machine world)))]\n        (is (empty? (:yin.k/frames body))\n            \"an explicit park mints no pending wait\")\n        (is (contains? (:yin.k/parked body) pid))\n        (is (= pid (:id (vm/value recv)))\n            \"the active park is the source's record, by its own id\")\n        (is (= (vm/value recv) (get (:parked recv) pid))))\n      :halted\n      (do (is (not (contains? body :yin.k/frames)))\n          (is (= (:value expected) (:yin.k/result body))\n              \"halt carries the result\")\n          (is (vm/halted? recv))\n          (is (empty? (:wait-set recv)))))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow every-corpus-segment-to-every-row-matches-the-reference\n  (slow/guard\n    \"every-corpus-segment-to-every-row-matches-the-reference\"\n    (fn []\n      (doseq [[engine version] lanes\n              [row build] rows\n              [seg wrap] corpus]\n        (testing (str (name engine) \" v\" version \" \" (name row) \" \" (name seg))\n          (let [expected (reference (build engine wrap))\n                world (build engine wrap)\n                {:keys [export lower recv relift] :as got}\n                (handed-off engine version world)\n                body (:body export)]\n            (is (:halted expected) \"the reference run completes\")\n            (check engine row :export (= :ok (:status export)) (pr-str export))\n            (when (= :ok (:status export))\n              (is (= (:kind world) (:kind export)))\n              (is (= version (:yin.k/version body)))\n              (kind-checks world expected export recv)\n              (is (= :ok (:status lower)) (pr-str lower))\n              (is (= :ok (:status relift)) (pr-str relift))\n              (check engine row :relift\n                     (= (s/stream-blind body) (s/stream-blind (:body relift)))\n                     \"lift(lower(frame)) reproduces the canonical body\")\n              (check engine row :result\n                     (= (select-keys expected [:halted :value :trace])\n                        (select-keys got [:halted :value :trace]))\n                     \"result and effect trace equal the reference run\"))))))))\n\n\n(deftest a-wait-over-a-live-host-primitive-resumes-on-every-profile\n  ;; no handoff: the reference machine alone, `conj` pending as an operand\n  (doseq [engine s/engines]\n    (testing (name engine)\n      (let [m0 (vm/run (s/load-ast\n                         engine (s/new-machine engine)\n                         (s/let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n                                 (s/let1 'c (s/cursor-of (s/v 's))\n                                         (s/app (s/v 'conj) (s/lit [])\n                                                (s/next-of (s/v 'c)))))))\n            _ (stream/append! (s/stream-of m0) \"A\")\n            done (try (vm/run m0)\n                      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) _\n                        nil))]\n        (check engine :live-primitive :resume\n               (and (some? done) (= [\"A\"] (vm/value done)))\n               \"the read wakes and the primitive applies\")))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Ordinary and tail effectful calls are what they claim\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest the-tail-rows-park-in-a-tail-call\n  (doseq [[row build] [[:ordinary-require (require-row false)]\n                       [:tail-require (require-row true)]\n                       [:ordinary-stream-call (stream-call-row false)]\n                       [:tail-stream-call (stream-call-row true)]]\n          [seg wrap] corpus]\n    (testing (str (name row) \" \" (name seg))\n      (let [m (:machine (build :semantic wrap))\n            entry (first (:wait-set m))\n            site (get-in m [:code (:segment entry) :code (dec (:pc entry))])]\n        (is (= (if (#{:tail-require :tail-stream-call} row)\n                 (:tailcall vm/opcode-table)\n                 (:call vm/opcode-table))\n               (first site))\n            (str \"the parking instruction \" (pr-str site)))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; One pc, two activations: distinct depth and captured environment\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- two-activations\n  \"One reading closure body, reached twice: through `g1` (captured\n   `:one`) as an operand, then through `g2` (captured `:two`) two\n   ordinary activations deeper.  Answers [parked source].\"\n  [engine]\n  (let [reader (s/lam ['k]\n                      (s/lam ['y]\n                             (cat-of (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'k)) (s/v 'y))\n                                     (s/next-of (s/v 'c)))))\n        body (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/app (s/v 'g1) (s/lit 1)))\n                     (nest 2 (s/app (s/v 'g2) (s/lit 2))))\n        m (vm/run\n            (s/load-ast\n              engine (s/new-machine engine)\n              (with-cat\n                (s/let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n                        (s/let1 'c (s/cursor-of (s/v 's))\n                                (s/let1 'mk reader\n                                        (s/let1 'g1 (s/app (s/v 'mk) (s/lit :one))\n                                                (s/let1 'g2 (s/app (s/v 'mk) (s/lit :two))\n                                                        body))))))))]\n    [m (s/stream-of m)]))\n\n\n(defn- registers\n  [export]\n  (get-in export [:body :yin.k/frames 0 :yin.k/registers]))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow one-pc-reached-at-two-depths-hands-off-at-each\n  (slow/guard\n    \"one-pc-reached-at-two-depths-hands-off-at-each\"\n    (fn []\n      (doseq [[engine version] lanes]\n        (testing (str (name engine) \" v\" version)\n          (let [[ref-m ref-src] (two-activations engine)\n                _ (stream/append! ref-src \"B\")\n                ref-hop (s/drive-local ref-m 6)\n                _ (stream/append! ref-src \"C\")\n                expected (vm/value (s/drive-local ref-hop 6))\n                [m src] (two-activations engine)\n                t1 (s/toy)\n                p1 (s/served-peer t1)\n                e1 (lift m version t1 p1 #{:reader})\n                r1 (:vm (handoff/resume-task\n                          (s/new-machine engine {:attach-stream (s/attacher t1)})\n                          (:bytes e1) (s/attacher t1) {:address (:address e1)}))\n                _ (stream/append! src \"B\")\n                hop (drive-peers r1 [p1] 6)\n                t2 (s/toy)\n                p2 (s/served-peer t2)\n                e2 (lift hop version t2 p2 #{:reader})\n                r2 (:vm (handoff/resume-task\n                          (s/new-machine engine {:attach-stream (s/attacher t2)})\n                          (:bytes e2) (s/attacher t2) {:address (:address e2)}))\n                _ (stream/append! src \"C\")\n                done (drive-peers r2 [p2 p1] 8)\n                regs1 (registers e1)\n                regs2 (registers e2)]\n            (is (= :ok (:status e1)) (pr-str e1))\n            (is (= :ok (:status e2)) (pr-str e2))\n            (is (= [:next :next] (mapv (comp :yin.k/reason frame-pending) [e1 e2])))\n            ;; the walker's frame is its environment and continuation alone:\n            ;; it has no pc to compare\n            (when-not (= :walker engine)\n              (is (some? (:yin.k/pc regs1)))\n              (is (= (select-keys regs1 [:yin.k/pc :yin.k/segment :yin.k/image])\n                     (select-keys regs2 [:yin.k/pc :yin.k/segment :yin.k/image]))\n                  \"both hand-offs park at one pc of one segment\"))\n            (is (not= regs1 regs2)\n                \"with a different activation: depth and captured environment\")\n            (is (= [[:one 1 \"B\"] [2 [1 [:two 2 \"C\"]]]] expected))\n            (is (vm/halted? done))\n            (is (= expected (vm/value done))\n                \"two hand-offs answer what the source's own run did\")))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Queued work, a shared response cursor, a held immediate, the writer\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- counting-server\n  [t peer surfaces]\n  (let [n (atom 0)\n        serve! (s/server peer (:channel t) surfaces)]\n    [(fn [h] (swap! n inc) (serve! h)) n]))\n\n\n(deftest a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-not-quiescent\n  (doseq [[engine version] lanes]\n    (testing (str (name engine) \" v\" version)\n      (let [[parked src] (s/parked-reader engine)\n            _ (stream/append! src \"B\")\n            woken (engine/check-wait-set parked)\n            t (s/toy)\n            [serve! n] (counting-server t (s/served-peer t) #{:reader})\n            r (handoff/export-task woken serve! (when (= 2 version) {:version 2}))]\n        (is (seq (:ready-queue woken)) \"the sweep queued the woken reader\")\n        (is (= :yin.k/not-quiescent (:yin.k/status r)) (pr-str r))\n        (is (not (contains? r :bytes)) \"nothing is published\")\n        (is (zero? @n) \"no stream was served\")))))\n\n\n(defn- two-callers\n  \"A sent caller whose response cell is shared by a second outstanding\n   call: the real waiter, and a second waiter built from it under its own\n   call id -- the construction of the stage-1 alias row.  Answers\n   [machine call-out].\"\n  [engine]\n  (let [[parked _ call-out] (s/parked-sent-caller engine)\n        e1 (first (:wait-set parked))\n        ;; the walker keeps the call id in its continuation as well\n        e2 (cond-> (assoc e1 :call-id :parked-9)\n             (contains? (:k e1) :call-id) (assoc-in [:k :call-id] :parked-9))]\n    [(assoc parked :wait-set [e1 e2]) call-out]))\n\n\n(defn- answer-both!\n  \"The second call's response first, then the first's.\"\n  [call-out]\n  (stream/append! call-out (apply2/success-response :parked-9 \"second\"))\n  (stream/append! call-out (apply2/success-response :parked-0 \"first\")))\n\n\n(defn- sweep\n  [m peers]\n  (loop [m (engine/check-wait-set m) n 12]\n    (if (or (zero? n) (empty? (:wait-set m)))\n      m\n      (do (run! s/serve-mirror! peers)\n          (recur (engine/check-wait-set m) (dec n))))))\n\n\n(deftest a-response-cursor-shared-by-two-waiters-crosses-as-one-cell\n  (doseq [[engine version] lanes]\n    (testing (str (name engine) \" v\" version)\n      (let [[ref-m ref-out] (two-callers engine)\n            _ (answer-both! ref-out)\n            expected (mapv :value (:ready-queue (sweep ref-m [])))\n            [m call-out] (two-callers engine)\n            t (s/toy)\n            peer (s/served-peer t)\n            export (lift m version t peer #{:reader})\n            pendings (mapv :yin.k/pending (get-in export [:body :yin.k/frames]))\n            own-out (s/ring 8)\n            recv (:vm (handoff/resume-task\n                        (s/new-machine engine {:attach-stream (s/attacher t)\n                                               :call-in (s/ring 8)\n                                               :call-out own-out\n                                               :call-out-cursor\n                                               (vm/mint-oldest own-out :test)})\n                        (:bytes export) (s/attacher t)\n                        {:address (:address export)}))\n            [w1 w2] (:wait-set recv)\n            _ (answer-both! call-out)\n            swept (sweep recv [peer])]\n        (is (= :ok (:status export)) (pr-str export))\n        (is (= [:ffi :ffi] (mapv :yin.k/reason pendings)))\n        (is (= [:parked-0 :parked-9] (mapv :yin.k/call-id pendings)))\n        (is (= 1 (count (get-in export [:body :yin.k/cells])))\n            \"the two waiters name one cell\")\n        (is (= (:cursor-ref w1) (:cursor-ref w2))\n            \"the lower gives both waiters one fresh cursor entry\")\n        (is (= [(apply2/success-response :parked-9 \"second\")\n                (apply2/success-response :parked-0 \"first\")]\n               expected)\n            \"the reference: each waiter woke on its own correlated response\")\n        (is (empty? (:wait-set swept)))\n        (is (= expected (mapv :value (:ready-queue swept)))\n            \"the receiver wakes the same waiters with the same responses\")))))\n\n\n(deftest a-held-immediate-refuses-export\n  (doseq [[engine version] lanes]\n    (testing (str (name engine) \" v\" version)\n      (let [m0 (s/load-ast engine (s/new-machine engine {:modules stream-modules})\n                           (s/app (s/v 'stream/poll!) (s/v 'c)))\n            [sref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 (s/ring 8))\n            [cref m2] (engine/handle-cursor m1 {:stream sref} :k1)\n            held (vm/run (assoc m2 :store {'c cref} :yin.k/gate :running))\n            t (s/toy)\n            [serve! n] (counting-server t (s/served-peer t) #{:reader})\n            r (handoff/export-task held serve! (when (= 2 version) {:version 2}))]\n        (is (= [:observe] (mapv :reason (:wait-set held)))\n            \"the gated poll is held as the D4 :observe entry\")\n        (is (= :yin.k/non-portable (:yin.k/status r)) (pr-str r))\n        (is (= :reason-mismatch (:yin.k/kind r)))\n        (is (= :observe (:yin.k/hold r)))\n        (is (not (contains? r :bytes)))\n        (is (zero? @n) \"refused before any stream was served\")))))\n\n\n(deftest a-lowered-writer-completes-only-on-source-acceptance\n  (doseq [[engine version] lanes]\n    (testing (str (name engine) \" v\" version)\n      (let [[parked w] (s/parked-writer engine)\n            t (s/toy)\n            peer (s/served-peer t)\n            export (lift parked version t peer #{:reader :writer})\n            recv (:vm (handoff/resume-task\n                        (s/new-machine engine {:attach-stream (s/attacher t)})\n                        (:bytes export) (s/attacher t)\n                        {:address (:address export)}))\n            ;; the source target stays full through the first drive\n            done (drive-peers recv [peer] 6)\n            _ (s/serve-mirror! peer)\n            held (stream/next w 0)\n            later (drive-peers done [peer] 6)\n            _ (s/serve-mirror! peer)\n            landed (stream/next w 0)]\n        (is (= :ok (:status export)) (pr-str export))\n        (is (= :warmed (:dao.stream/value held)))\n        (check engine :writer :source-acceptance (vm/blocked? done)\n               \"the retry stays parked while the source refuses it\")\n        (check engine :writer :source-acceptance\n               (and (vm/halted? later) (= \"v\" (:dao.stream/value landed)))\n               \"once the source accepts, the retained value lands\")))))\n","numLines":727,"startLine":1,"totalLines":727}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RTyrQES6dphLHR6MCiifye","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
