{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TXv4mRcWCearWpRcPPTjZy","type":"tool_result","content":"(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.clj*\n1:(ns yin.vm.ucf.remote\n2-  \"The UCF facade through `dao.stream.remote` descriptors: lifts a\n3-   parked semantic machine's pending wait\n4-   (`docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` S7.4.3) into\n5-   UCF data whose cells and stream markers name `dao.stream.remote`\n6-   descriptors under the `:dao.stream.remote/v1` cursor profile\n7-   (S7.5.3), and lowers that data back into a resumable local wait\n8-   through a reflection (`docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md` S2.2,\n9-   S2.4).\n10-\n11-   The local side is the engine's own parked machinery, not an\n12-   invented shape. A pending entry is what `yin.vm` parks: the\n13-   machine registers beside `:stream-id` and `:cursor-ref`\n359:(defn primitive-function\n438:(defn profile-of\n446:(defn name-of\n499:(def call-in-stream-key\n504:(def call-out-stream-key\n509:(def call-out-cursor-key\n148:(defn response-wait-entry\n149-  \"The polling wait entry for a sent call awaiting its correlated response,\n150-   for an arbitrary register payload (`yin.vm.engine.md` section 7, edit 3).\n151-\n152-   `entry` is a wait, ready, or parked record as the VM built it: the\n153-   writer entry that retried the request, or the registers of a call whose\n154-   request was sent at once. The FFI keys of the writer step\n155-   (`:request-sent`, `:op`) and its retried `:datom` are removed; the\n156-   call-out reader keys are added. Every other key -- the VM's register\n157-   payload, whatever its shape -- is preserved verbatim, so no VM has to\n158-   know this layout. `call-response-wait-entry` (the walker's frame-typed\n159-   shape) is unchanged.\"\n160-  [entry call-id]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee657710-cc1c-4c43-882b-5874c9a79051","uuid":"73af384b-1bad-45d0-8ab1-888ac854d78f","timestamp":"2026-10-12T15: