{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxeYMeyGWCqiEXMNtZ5e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Slice 6b is implemented and green on the JVM, and all six mutants are caught. Nothing is committed, and Node and Dart were not run. The report is at `collab/1792270000000-engineer-6b-task-transport.report.md`.\n\n**Step 0:** every prerequisite named in 8.2 is on the branch: the kernel's linking methods and retained `free-env` field, the `scan` namespace over v4 vectors, and the 4b stage-2 FFI, link and install behaviour. I built none of them.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **`rows.cljc`** (+612): `lift-task` and `lower-task`. The lift takes `:free-env` as an override and otherwise uses the kernel's field; it refuses `:missing-free-env` only when neither exists.\n- **Lower:** all checks (gate through frames, then pendings, dependencies and custody for every task including install children) run before the first `attach!`. It then restores waits, parked records, store, module stores, install children and the free environment, and runs nothing.\n- **`safepoint_harness_test.cljc`** (new, 963 lines): acceptance items 1–8. It asserts the 89-run count, and each run checks laws 1, 2, 3 and 6.\n- **`store_write_audit_test.clj`**: two allowlist entries for the lower's store write, which goes through `engine/store-put` the same way the handoff lower does.\n\n**Results:**\n- **Harness:** quick tier 13 tests and 357 assertions; slow matrix 1 test, 89 runs, 609 assertions.\n- **Wider sweep:** all 54 `yin.vm.ucf.*` and `yin.vm.semantic-register.*` namespaces pass, 830 tests. That sweep ran just before I added two final assertions to the harness; the harness was rerun green afterwards and `rows.cljc` had not changed since.\n- **kondo:** clean on all three changed files.\n- **Not done:** item 9's three-host `bb test:sub yin.vm`.\n\n**Mutants:** all six are caught (tail lowered with a window, first-defect ordering, a dropped pending restoration, double delivery into the captured `rd`, attaching before refusing, ignoring the `:free-env` override). Two of them were only caught after I added an assertion each: a check that the lowered tail entry has no window, and a refusal that happens after decode (a segment with no tree association).\n\n**Design bugs found** (design text not changed):\n- **Rows 10 and 11:** the install states they describe can't be reached at a safepoint. A blocked child is always at phase `:parked`, and a child that executes `:park` either completes the install or is refused. I used the engine's real state for row 10, and the same state with the phase set to `:running` by hand for row 11. An Architect should rewrite both rows.\n- **Row 21 under `:depth-3`:** the `nest` wrapper's own parameter is named `x`, so the result is `[3 [2 [1 1]]]`, not 99. The lowered run matches the reference; I pinned that one case to 1.\n- **The `:tail` fourth-slot refusal:** the codec refuses it as `:row-shape` at the structure step, before the frame validator could report `:frame-shape`. The test asserts `:row-shape`.\n- **§7.1 order:** the dependency closure can only run after the walk, because the segments aren't known until then.\n\n**Deviations you should know about:**\n- **Tree association:** the kernel has no source index, so the lift takes it as a `:source-index` option from the caller.\n- **Linked modules:** registry entries don't travel in the carrier, so row 17's receiver is given the source's registry.\n- **Custody:** a lift always carries none; the lower refuses a carrier with custody as `:yin.k/unsupported`.\n- **Other:** refusals are thrown, matching the rest of the codec, and the whole store is carried.\n- **Possible bug in `handoff.cljc` (not edited):** it builds installing names with `(symbol (str m \"/\" x))`, which never equals `m/x`.\n\nNo git command was blocked."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_